WEBVTT

1
00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:23.833
[birds calling]

2
00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:30.750
[woman] <i>Kolappalur,</i>
<i>even the people of Tamil Nadu</i>

3
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:32.791
<i>have no clue where this village is.</i>

4
00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:34.375
<i>It's so remote</i>

5
00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:36.583
<i>that there's</i>
<i>no cellphone signal there either.</i>

6
00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:37.958
[serene music playing]

7
00:00:42.416 --> 00:00:46.083
<i>In that very small village,</i>
<i>there lived a girl with a big dream.</i>

8
00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:47.916
<i>You know what her dream was?</i>

9
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.750
<i>To go to Korea.</i>

10
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:52.625
{\an8}<i>She wanted to visit Korea</i>
<i>at least once in her life.</i>

11
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:57.041
[pleasant music playing]

12
00:01:32.916 --> 00:01:34.333
[music continues]

13
00:01:55.916 --> 00:01:57.458
[alarm ringing]

14
00:01:57.541 --> 00:01:59.125
[upbeat music playing]

15
00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:12.708
{\an8}♪ <i>Every eye is dreamin' ♪</i>

16
00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.666
<i>♪ Life keeps something brewin' ♪</i>

17
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.458
[in Korean] One bite, one bite,
just try one bite!

18
00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:20.291
{\an8}<i>♪ New roads keep appearin' ♪</i>

19
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.333
{\an8}<i>♪ Heartbeats keep on thumpin' ♪</i>

20
00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:23.416
{\an8}[in Korean] Take care!

21
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.958
{\an8}Yes, I'm just walking down. Yes.

22
00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:27.333
I'll be there in a bit.
Okay, see you soon!

23
00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:31.208
<i>♪ Journey callin'</i>
<i>Fervy movin' ♪</i>

24
00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:34.166
{\an8}<i>♪ Closer to many riz ♪</i>

25
00:02:35.708 --> 00:02:38.833
{\an8}<i>♪ I need this swirl to chill ♪</i>

26
00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.958
{\an8}<i>♪ Allow to take ma quill ♪</i>

27
00:02:41.041 --> 00:02:44.583
{\an8}[both in English] Yay! Finally,
we are going to meet Shenba! Whoo!

28
00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:47.333
[woman] <i>So if I tell you</i>
<i>that four people from Korea</i>

29
00:02:47.416 --> 00:02:50.833
<i>are coming to see</i>
<i>that village girl with a big dream,</i>

30
00:02:50.916 --> 00:02:52.208
<i>would you believe me?</i>

31
00:02:55.416 --> 00:02:58.458
<i>My name is Shenba. Shenbagam.</i>

32
00:02:58.541 --> 00:03:00.083
<i>I want to take a flight someday.</i>

33
00:03:00.166 --> 00:03:02.500
<i>I want to fly to my favorite place, Korea.</i>

34
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:05.250
<i>Do you know why I started</i>
<i>dreaming about this place?</i>

35
00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:06.583
<i>Because of my school play.</i>

36
00:03:06.666 --> 00:03:08.166
<i>While Miss Matilda made us play</i>

37
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.541
<i>Subramania Bharathi, Subhash Chandra Bose,</i>

38
00:03:10.625 --> 00:03:12.166
<i>Mother Teresa…</i>

39
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.416
<i>I chose to be her… Shenbavalam.</i>

40
00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:17.583
<i>Don't know who I'm talking about?</i>

41
00:03:17.666 --> 00:03:19.666
<i>Even I didn't know her until the play.</i>

42
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.750
<i>It's the story of a Tamil girl</i>

43
00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:23.916
<i>who travels from Kanniyakumari to Korea.</i>

44
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:30.083
<i>If I told you that the culture</i>
<i>and traditions of Tamil Nadu,</i>

45
00:03:30.166 --> 00:03:32.166
<i>along with the countless Tamil words,</i>

46
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.916
<i>are in use in Korea to this day,</i>
<i>would you believe it?</i>

47
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.833
<i>The reason for that is none other</i>
<i>than Queen Senbavalam.</i>

48
00:03:39.916 --> 00:03:43.583
<i>Everybody saw me as that queen that day</i>
<i>and I got a standing ovation.</i>

49
00:03:43.666 --> 00:03:46.458
<i>You should have seen my father.</i>
<i>He was so happy.</i>

50
00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:48.083
[pleasant music playing]

51
00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:52.958
By the way, Shenbavalam,
yesterday in that school play,

52
00:03:53.041 --> 00:03:55.375
you really killed it
with that queen costume.

53
00:03:55.458 --> 00:03:56.458
Well done! [chuckles]

54
00:03:56.541 --> 00:03:57.833
[in Korean] <i>Gamsahabnida.</i>

55
00:03:57.916 --> 00:03:58.958
[in English] Hi, Shenbavalam.

56
00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:01.041
Go, Shenbavalam.

57
00:04:01.125 --> 00:04:04.416
[Shenbagam] <i>After that day, everyone</i>
<i>started calling me "Shenbavalam".</i>

58
00:04:09.875 --> 00:04:12.375
<i>I started learning</i>
<i>a lot about the Korean culture.</i>

59
00:04:12.458 --> 00:04:14.333
<i>I even started learning the language.</i>

60
00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:16.666
[playful music playing]

61
00:04:18.208 --> 00:04:19.208
Uh…

62
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:30.583
[in Korean] Gomavo… Gomawoyo!

63
00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:33.458
Mianhae… Mianhaeyo.

64
00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:36.125
[in English]
Hey, what the hell are you blabbering?

65
00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:37.208
Shh.

66
00:04:37.291 --> 00:04:38.958
Learning English. [grunts]

67
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.625
Shenba!

68
00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:43.541
-Yes?
-Play it loud

69
00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:44.958
so that we can also hear the song.

70
00:04:45.041 --> 00:04:46.083
You won't understand this song.

71
00:04:46.166 --> 00:04:47.458
Are you listening to hip-hop?

72
00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:49.708
Mm-hm. It's K-pop!

73
00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:51.875
[Shenbagam] <i>This is Mani.</i>

74
00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:56.333
<i>I loved him… as much as I loved</i>
<i>the idea of going to Korea.</i>

75
00:04:58.708 --> 00:05:01.083
I have to get to Korea somehow.

76
00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:02.250
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

77
00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:03.583
I'll tell you how to get there.

78
00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:04.708
Okay, tell me.

79
00:05:04.791 --> 00:05:07.708
[Mani] <i>Go to a local railway station,</i>
<i>get a ticket to Korea,</i>

80
00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:10.416
<i>hop on the train, and on you're own way.</i>

81
00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.875
Sir, what time is the train to Korea?

82
00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:16.000
[man] <i>Korea go to Platform One.</i>
<i>The train will come in half an hour.</i>

83
00:05:16.083 --> 00:05:19.041
Have you lost your mind?
How can you go to Korea by train?

84
00:05:19.125 --> 00:05:22.125
I don't know, Dad. My classmate Mani
told me to that the train--

85
00:05:22.208 --> 00:05:24.000
Forget what he said.
Don't you have a brain?

86
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:25.750
Idiot! Idiot! Idiot!

87
00:05:26.416 --> 00:05:28.125
Can I have two more idlis, please?

88
00:05:29.166 --> 00:05:32.125
Listen! Just call me if you need anything.

89
00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:33.750
Don't disturb my daughter.

90
00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.708
Shenba, go and manage the counter.

91
00:05:35.791 --> 00:05:37.958
[Shenbagam]
<i>My dad had a very simple dream.</i>

92
00:05:38.041 --> 00:05:41.000
<i>He wanted to hand over his eatery</i>
<i>to me when I grew up,</i>

93
00:05:41.083 --> 00:05:43.625
<i>and turn this place</i>
<i>into a fancy restaurant.</i>

94
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.166
Tenth grade is almost done, guys.
What are your plans?

95
00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.333
I'm going to join
a computer science group.

96
00:05:49.958 --> 00:05:51.291
Science. Doctor.

97
00:05:51.375 --> 00:05:52.916
I'm still thinking.

98
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.041
Mmm.

99
00:05:55.083 --> 00:05:57.833
Do you guys know any group I can join
where I can make lots of money?

100
00:05:59.791 --> 00:06:01.583
Why are you staring at me?

101
00:06:01.666 --> 00:06:03.291
I'm going to travel to Korea.

102
00:06:03.375 --> 00:06:04.583
Oh, really? By train?

103
00:06:04.666 --> 00:06:06.083
[all laugh]

104
00:06:06.875 --> 00:06:08.791
[Shenbagam]
<i>Because of my obsession with Korea,</i>

105
00:06:08.875 --> 00:06:10.666
<i>my mom and dad would often have fights.</i>

106
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.833
<i>Dad would say, "Just calm down.</i>
<i>She'll forget about it when she grows up."</i>

107
00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:15.000
[train horn honking]

108
00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:18.458
<i>But I didn't forget anything.</i>

109
00:06:18.541 --> 00:06:22.708
<i>In fact, as I grew older,</i>
<i>my desire to go to Korea grew stronger.</i>

110
00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:27.791
<i>Just like me,</i>
<i>my dad had his own dream, too.</i>

111
00:06:27.875 --> 00:06:31.375
<i>Since he wanted me to convert</i>
<i>his eatery into a fancy restaurant,</i>

112
00:06:31.458 --> 00:06:35.750
<i>he sent me to a college in a nearby town</i>
<i>to study hotel management.</i>

113
00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:37.458
You don't have
a single asset in your name.

114
00:06:37.541 --> 00:06:38.625
What do I keep as collateral?

115
00:06:38.708 --> 00:06:41.291
Sir, I really have to get to Korea.
Please approve my loan.

116
00:06:41.375 --> 00:06:43.875
All right, let's say
I approve this loan for you.

117
00:06:43.958 --> 00:06:46.083
-You will go and settle down in Korea.
-[bell rings]

118
00:06:46.166 --> 00:06:47.833
How will I collect on the loan?

119
00:06:47.916 --> 00:06:49.416
Do you expect me to follow you there?

120
00:06:52.083 --> 00:06:53.125
[chants prayers]

121
00:06:53.208 --> 00:06:54.500
Is there something else I can do?

122
00:06:55.125 --> 00:06:56.375
Well, there is another way.

123
00:06:59.958 --> 00:07:03.833
You could apply for an education loan,
get a student visa, and study in Korea.

124
00:07:03.916 --> 00:07:05.041
Then I'll think about it.

125
00:07:06.291 --> 00:07:07.291
Hmm.

126
00:07:07.375 --> 00:07:08.791
You know what I don't understand?

127
00:07:08.875 --> 00:07:10.750
You're taking such a big loan
to go to Korea.

128
00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:11.833
What's so special about it?

129
00:07:13.541 --> 00:07:15.750
Sir, tell me who's your favorite hero?

130
00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.916
Why did you get married to your wife?

131
00:07:18.458 --> 00:07:21.208
Why did you choose
to be a manager in this bank?

132
00:07:21.291 --> 00:07:24.208
Some questions are best left unanswered.

133
00:07:24.291 --> 00:07:25.541
I want to go there, that's all.

134
00:07:25.625 --> 00:07:26.833
[Manager scoffs]

135
00:07:26.916 --> 00:07:28.291
You sure have an attitude.

136
00:07:28.375 --> 00:07:29.416
Who's Shenbagam here?

137
00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.791
That's my daughter. What's the matter?

138
00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:40.583
You said our daughter will
support us when we get older.

139
00:07:40.666 --> 00:07:42.750
She went to Coimbatore
to apply for a passport.

140
00:07:42.833 --> 00:07:45.750
We live together, but she doesn't think
it's important tell us anything.

141
00:07:45.833 --> 00:07:49.291
Such double standards.
Do you tell her everything, too? Tell me?

142
00:07:49.375 --> 00:07:50.791
If she gets a job in Korea,

143
00:07:50.875 --> 00:07:52.708
I'm sure they're going to fire her
on the first day.

144
00:07:52.791 --> 00:07:55.208
Mom! If you have something to say,
say it to my face.

145
00:07:55.291 --> 00:07:56.916
Oh, you really think I'm scared of you?

146
00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.166
[Shenbagam scoffs]

147
00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.958
Look at your father. All he thinks about
is his restaurant and his house.

148
00:08:02.041 --> 00:08:04.000
Exactly. She doesn't
want to end up like him,

149
00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:05.708
that's why she's flying off to Korea.

150
00:08:05.791 --> 00:08:07.958
-Hey, mind your own business.
-[scoffs]

151
00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.208
Ask her what she's up to now.

152
00:08:10.875 --> 00:08:13.166
-Just go inside.
-Okay, I'll go.

153
00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.500
But instead of just
calling your daughter a queen,

154
00:08:15.583 --> 00:08:17.708
think of finding a suitable match for her.

155
00:08:17.791 --> 00:08:19.291
[melancholy music playing]

156
00:08:23.583 --> 00:08:27.791
Listen Shenba, I'm not as
young and healthy I used to be.

157
00:08:27.875 --> 00:08:29.958
I thought after getting you married

158
00:08:30.041 --> 00:08:33.041
I would hand over the restaurant
to you and retire peacefully.

159
00:08:33.125 --> 00:08:36.250
Then two random people walked in,
asking me if you were my daughter.

160
00:08:36.333 --> 00:08:37.875
Do you know how much that scared me?

161
00:08:37.958 --> 00:08:40.166
-Dad--
-Whatever you want to do,

162
00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.250
at least tell me.

163
00:08:42.875 --> 00:08:44.041
Think about it.

164
00:08:44.125 --> 00:08:46.708
[upbeat music playing]

165
00:09:01.833 --> 00:09:03.083
[cell phone buzzing]

166
00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:05.166
You're welcome, sir.

167
00:09:14.375 --> 00:09:16.083
[automated voice]
<i>The person you have called…</i>

168
00:09:20.041 --> 00:09:21.291
[cell phone buzzing]

169
00:09:23.625 --> 00:09:24.958
<i>The person you have called…</i>

170
00:09:29.958 --> 00:09:31.958
What the hell is wrong with this man?

171
00:09:32.041 --> 00:09:33.041
Hello?

172
00:09:33.125 --> 00:09:34.875
[man] <i>Hey, Mani, when the hell</i>
<i>are you going to pay me back?</i>

173
00:09:34.958 --> 00:09:36.833
I can't pay you back right now, sir.

174
00:09:36.916 --> 00:09:39.083
You came to the bank
begging me for a loan--

175
00:09:39.166 --> 00:09:41.625
Yeah, I made a mistake.
Taking a loan from you was a mistake.

176
00:09:41.708 --> 00:09:43.458
{\an8}If you don't pay up what you owe,

177
00:09:43.541 --> 00:09:46.666
then I'll make sure to come there and
I'll humiliate you in front of everyone.

178
00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.166
[clicks tongue]

179
00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.250
Sir, sorry, sir.

180
00:09:49.333 --> 00:09:51.583
<i>I'll try and pay you back</i>
<i>in a week anyhow.</i>

181
00:09:51.666 --> 00:09:53.333
{\an8}Now I want the entire amount.

182
00:09:53.416 --> 00:09:54.416
<i>Hang up now!</i>

183
00:09:58.916 --> 00:10:00.583
[melancholy music playing]

184
00:10:07.208 --> 00:10:08.458
[footsteps approaching]

185
00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:09.750
Hey.

186
00:10:09.833 --> 00:10:10.916
What is it?

187
00:10:11.958 --> 00:10:13.708
How long are you going
to keep avoiding me, Mani?

188
00:10:13.791 --> 00:10:15.791
You really think I'm avoiding you?

189
00:10:15.875 --> 00:10:17.250
Can't you see I'm busy working?

190
00:10:17.333 --> 00:10:18.583
Oh, is that so?

191
00:10:18.666 --> 00:10:20.291
[sighs] Never mind.

192
00:10:21.125 --> 00:10:22.416
When are you going to come
talk to my father?

193
00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.791
[Mani sighs]

194
00:10:23.875 --> 00:10:25.833
What do you want me
to come and tell your father?

195
00:10:25.916 --> 00:10:28.416
{\an8}That I serve drinks and sing
in a bar for a living?

196
00:10:28.916 --> 00:10:31.375
All my friends have made it big in life.

197
00:10:31.458 --> 00:10:33.666
Just look at me.
I'm struggling. I'm stuck over here.

198
00:10:34.625 --> 00:10:37.625
And my father's debts…
they just keep piling up on my head.

199
00:10:38.541 --> 00:10:39.958
And you expect me to forget about it?

200
00:10:47.125 --> 00:10:48.166
Listen, I'm sorry.

201
00:10:49.125 --> 00:10:51.291
Please give me some time.
I'll talk to your father soon.

202
00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.250
I'll fix everything and come get you.

203
00:10:54.333 --> 00:10:56.125
Whenever I'm mad and come talk to you,

204
00:10:56.208 --> 00:10:59.208
you say something like this
and I just forget about everything.

205
00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:00.458
[sighs heavily]

206
00:11:03.041 --> 00:11:04.500
We fought about this a hundred times.

207
00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.625
More like a thousand times.

208
00:11:08.125 --> 00:11:09.125
[Tamil song playing]

209
00:12:02.958 --> 00:12:05.041
[Mani] <i>Remember I told you</i>
<i>about a friend in Mumbai?</i>

210
00:12:05.125 --> 00:12:07.000
I've been planning
to start a business with him.

211
00:12:07.083 --> 00:12:08.916
If it goes well,
it will all work out fine.

212
00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.166
-[cell phone buzzing]
-Look, that's him. One second.

213
00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.583
Hey, are you hungry?

214
00:12:56.166 --> 00:12:58.833
-I'll call you when it's ready. Relax.
-Bloody stupid.

215
00:12:58.916 --> 00:12:59.833
[clicks tongue]

216
00:13:01.083 --> 00:13:03.375
It's boiling, it's boiling.
Be careful, careful.

217
00:13:34.083 --> 00:13:36.500
Listen. Boys your age
have all found good jobs

218
00:13:36.583 --> 00:13:38.416
and settled in Chennai and Bangalore.

219
00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.208
Why don't you also look for a job there?

220
00:13:42.041 --> 00:13:43.125
Sir…

221
00:13:43.208 --> 00:13:45.500
with all due respect,
I know what I'm doing with my life.

222
00:13:53.291 --> 00:13:56.750
Shenba, you haven't taken your eyes
off your phone even for a minute.

223
00:13:56.833 --> 00:13:57.958
You so disrespectful.

224
00:13:59.291 --> 00:14:00.541
She doesn't really care.

225
00:14:00.625 --> 00:14:02.375
Mom, what the hell is your problem?

226
00:14:02.458 --> 00:14:03.458
Every time we come here

227
00:14:03.541 --> 00:14:05.750
you keep saying that you're
about to get your daughter married.

228
00:14:05.833 --> 00:14:07.458
But it doesn't seem
like it'll ever happen.

229
00:14:07.541 --> 00:14:08.666
-Aunty.
-Huh?

230
00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:10.791
You're here for the festival.
Have a good time,

231
00:14:10.875 --> 00:14:12.458
enjoy the food, and leave.

232
00:14:12.541 --> 00:14:13.541
[scoffing]

233
00:14:15.625 --> 00:14:16.791
Listen to me.

234
00:14:16.875 --> 00:14:19.250
Look for a nice boy for her
and get her married.

235
00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:21.250
[Shenbagam scoffs]

236
00:14:24.041 --> 00:14:25.375
[quirky music playing]

237
00:14:33.583 --> 00:14:35.625
Mom, why are you doing this?
You know I don't want to--

238
00:14:35.708 --> 00:14:37.583
Why, what's wrong?
They're just here to see you.

239
00:14:37.666 --> 00:14:39.166
They'll meet you and then leave.

240
00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.708
We'll talk about all of this later.

241
00:14:40.791 --> 00:14:43.625
Right now, I just want you to put on
some makeup and get ready.

242
00:14:43.708 --> 00:14:45.500
Just wants to argue all the time.

243
00:14:52.666 --> 00:14:53.708
The weather is really nice.

244
00:14:54.458 --> 00:14:56.416
Just like Bangalore. But it's colder here.

245
00:14:57.958 --> 00:14:59.416
I studied in Ooty.

246
00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:02.625
Engineering, IT job, monthly 90k salary.
I have a car, too.

247
00:15:03.666 --> 00:15:05.250
You don't care about all this. I know.

248
00:15:07.083 --> 00:15:09.750
Two days ago at the festival,
your father saw you with some other guy.

249
00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:12.291
He told me this yesterday

250
00:15:12.375 --> 00:15:14.000
because he wanted me to know
everything about you.

251
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.208
And I have no problem with that.

252
00:15:17.541 --> 00:15:19.083
He also told me that you love Korea.

253
00:15:20.583 --> 00:15:23.166
No problem.
I'll take you to Korea for a honeymoon.

254
00:15:23.875 --> 00:15:24.875
Only if you say yes to me.

255
00:15:29.333 --> 00:15:30.333
Okay.

256
00:15:30.416 --> 00:15:33.416
I get it. I'll go down and figure out
how to put an end to this.

257
00:15:35.166 --> 00:15:36.791
[Shenbagam]
<i>He said he'll put an end to this.</i>

258
00:15:36.875 --> 00:15:38.625
<i>Told me not to worry about anything.</i>

259
00:15:38.708 --> 00:15:40.875
<i>But instead, he said yes to the marriage.</i>

260
00:15:40.958 --> 00:15:42.833
{\an8}[melancholy music paying]

261
00:15:44.625 --> 00:15:47.583
Hey, what do you want now?
What the hell's wrong with you?

262
00:15:47.666 --> 00:15:49.083
You really don't know
what's wrong with me?

263
00:15:49.166 --> 00:15:50.166
How would I know?

264
00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:51.833
I thought my family
was just messing with me,

265
00:15:51.916 --> 00:15:53.333
but they're serious about my marriage.

266
00:15:53.416 --> 00:15:55.375
How long are we going
to meet each other like this, Mani?

267
00:15:55.458 --> 00:15:57.666
You wanted to go to Korea.
Where did marriage come from?

268
00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.416
Korea is my dream and I will get there.

269
00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.708
That doesn't mean that
I'm never going to get married.

270
00:16:01.791 --> 00:16:03.291
Listen to me.

271
00:16:03.375 --> 00:16:04.375
Give me some time.

272
00:16:04.458 --> 00:16:06.291
All I'm asking for is time.
I'll sort everything out.

273
00:16:06.375 --> 00:16:08.833
-Please, just come and talk to my father.
-Just try and understand.

274
00:16:08.916 --> 00:16:11.208
I'm sure if you talk to him
things will work out for us.

275
00:16:11.291 --> 00:16:12.333
Please.

276
00:16:13.208 --> 00:16:14.375
-Please-- [gasps]
-Shenba!

277
00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.541
[dramatic music playing]

278
00:16:17.625 --> 00:16:19.500
-What are you doing here?
-Dad?

279
00:16:19.583 --> 00:16:20.833
-How dare you!
-[Shenbagam gasps]

280
00:16:20.916 --> 00:16:23.666
-Dad!
-I saw you at the temple and I knew it.

281
00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.250
But I never thought that
it would come to this.

282
00:16:25.333 --> 00:16:27.958
Dad, just listen to what
he has to say. Please, Dad.

283
00:16:28.041 --> 00:16:29.166
Let's hear it, then.

284
00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.333
What you want to say?

285
00:16:30.416 --> 00:16:32.875
You work in a bar,
and you want to marry my daughter?

286
00:16:32.958 --> 00:16:34.416
-You have nothing to your name.
-Dad.

287
00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.666
You're crossing the line, sir.

288
00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:37.375
Where will she live?
On the streets, like you?

289
00:16:37.458 --> 00:16:39.916
Dad, let go of him, please.
Just hear him out once.

290
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.708
-Shenba, come with me. Let's go.
-Dad!

291
00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.000
[melancholy music playing]

292
00:16:48.083 --> 00:16:49.833
-Dad…
-Am I nothing to you?

293
00:16:50.708 --> 00:16:51.708
Please don't say that, Dad.

294
00:16:54.875 --> 00:16:57.333
-So you don't care anymore.
-Dad, it's not like that.

295
00:17:01.916 --> 00:17:02.916
Dad!

296
00:17:03.583 --> 00:17:05.625
You're going to regret this.
Take my word for it.

297
00:17:10.916 --> 00:17:11.958
Are you happy now?

298
00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:14.958
You wanted him to humiliate me?

299
00:17:19.833 --> 00:17:22.291
Shenba, you want to be with me, right?

300
00:17:22.375 --> 00:17:23.666
Then listen to me carefully.

301
00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:24.750
Just come with me.

302
00:17:24.833 --> 00:17:26.833
But you can't ask where I'm taking to you.
You understand?

303
00:17:26.916 --> 00:17:29.083
You will never question me again.
Do you get it?

304
00:17:29.166 --> 00:17:32.541
[Shenbagam] <i>I went along with</i>
<i>whatever he said, no questions asked.</i>

305
00:17:32.625 --> 00:17:34.333
<i>That's the kind of trust I had in him.</i>

306
00:17:35.083 --> 00:17:36.500
[train honks]

307
00:17:38.916 --> 00:17:40.750
[pleasant music playing]

308
00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:44.250
<i>It was a new place.</i>
<i>I didn't know anybody there.</i>

309
00:17:44.333 --> 00:17:45.333
<i>Except for him.</i>

310
00:17:48.541 --> 00:17:49.875
[inaudible]

311
00:17:50.833 --> 00:17:52.291
Now go and get ready. I'll be back soon.

312
00:17:58.625 --> 00:18:00.916
<i>We both didn't know</i>
<i>what the future holds for us.</i>

313
00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.916
<i>We had no clue what would happen next.</i>

314
00:18:05.208 --> 00:18:09.041
<i>For the first time I was away from home,</i>
<i>away from my dad.</i>

315
00:18:09.125 --> 00:18:10.333
<i>I felt lonely.</i>

316
00:18:15.541 --> 00:18:18.708
<i>But I knew in my heart</i>
<i>that Dad would only be thinking about me.</i>

317
00:18:18.791 --> 00:18:20.083
[gentle music playing]

318
00:18:20.166 --> 00:18:21.500
[gentle music continues]

319
00:18:31.541 --> 00:18:32.791
[waves lapping]

320
00:18:39.375 --> 00:18:40.833
[Šenbagam] I think I should go back.

321
00:18:40.916 --> 00:18:42.250
We're in this because of me.

322
00:18:42.333 --> 00:18:43.958
But I don't know how I'll face my dad.

323
00:18:44.041 --> 00:18:45.500
Why do you want to go back?

324
00:18:46.166 --> 00:18:47.333
Now listen to me.

325
00:18:54.625 --> 00:18:56.333
Your life will be ruined
if you stay with me,

326
00:18:56.416 --> 00:18:57.958
keeps playing again and again in my head.

327
00:18:58.916 --> 00:19:01.083
That's why we're going to move to Korea.

328
00:19:02.041 --> 00:19:04.541
We'll find jobs there,
and we'll live there.

329
00:19:05.916 --> 00:19:08.083
What are you talking about?
I don't get it.

330
00:19:08.708 --> 00:19:11.208
Listen, financially you're
struggling a lot, I know.

331
00:19:12.791 --> 00:19:16.166
I know Korea is my dream,
but let it be for now.

332
00:19:17.375 --> 00:19:21.000
At the moment we need to pay our bills.
You need to find a job. I need a job.

333
00:19:21.083 --> 00:19:23.750
If we work over here,
then all we'll do is survive.

334
00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:27.083
You don't need to worry about the money.
I'll manage.

335
00:19:27.166 --> 00:19:28.708
I've applied for our passports.

336
00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:32.333
It's a good agency.
All legal formalities are complete.

337
00:19:32.416 --> 00:19:33.791
We'll get the passport soon.

338
00:19:34.375 --> 00:19:36.750
And over there,
there's a job waiting for you

339
00:19:36.833 --> 00:19:37.750
at a five-star hotel.

340
00:19:37.833 --> 00:19:40.083
The agency said they'll take care of it,

341
00:19:40.166 --> 00:19:42.208
and that you'll get an official
job offer letter.

342
00:19:43.875 --> 00:19:45.583
At least your job is confirmed.

343
00:19:45.666 --> 00:19:46.916
I'll find a job too.

344
00:19:51.625 --> 00:19:53.958
It's so hard living here without my dad.

345
00:19:54.791 --> 00:19:58.166
I don't know how I'm going to live
without him in Korea. Please.

346
00:20:01.583 --> 00:20:03.083
Look, Shenba.

347
00:20:03.166 --> 00:20:06.791
We've known each other for nine years.
Just trust me.

348
00:20:07.541 --> 00:20:10.458
[Shenbagam] <i>If he said something,</i>
<i>I just believed him.</i>

349
00:20:10.541 --> 00:20:12.041
<i>I really don't know why.</i>

350
00:20:12.125 --> 00:20:15.958
<i>Just as he had said,</i>
<i>25 days later, we left for Korea.</i>

351
00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:19.708
[siren wailing]

352
00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.041
-Hello, are you done with your work?
-Hello.

353
00:20:31.125 --> 00:20:32.791
It's going to take little longer.

354
00:20:32.875 --> 00:20:35.083
<i>I need to exchange money.</i>
<i>I'll be there soon.</i>

355
00:20:35.166 --> 00:20:37.041
[gentle music playing]

356
00:20:48.958 --> 00:20:49.958
I'm almost there. Coming.

357
00:20:50.041 --> 00:20:51.833
<i>You go ahead and check-in.</i>
<i>I'm almost there.</i>

358
00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:04.166
[female announcer] <i>Dear passengers,</i>

359
00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:06.708
<i>as we prepare to head towards</i>
<i>the Korean Peninsula,</i>

360
00:21:06.791 --> 00:21:09.458
<i>please ensure your seatbelts</i>
<i>are securely fastened.</i>

361
00:21:09.541 --> 00:21:11.208
<i>and your seats and tray tables</i>

362
00:21:11.291 --> 00:21:13.541
<i>are in their full upright</i>
<i>and stowed position.</i>

363
00:21:13.625 --> 00:21:15.458
{\an8}-Hello?
-[Mani] <i>I'm coming. Just two minutes.</i>

364
00:21:15.541 --> 00:21:17.750
{\an8}-Where the hell are you?
<i>-I'm in the airport. Just hang on.</i>

365
00:21:19.041 --> 00:21:20.500
I've already boarded the aircraft.

366
00:21:20.583 --> 00:21:22.041
<i>Okay, okay, relax. I'm coming. I'm coming.</i>

367
00:21:22.958 --> 00:21:24.291
[phone beeps]

368
00:21:24.375 --> 00:21:25.666
[suspenseful music playing]

369
00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:35.666
[cell phone ringing]

370
00:21:46.375 --> 00:21:47.375
Hello?

371
00:21:49.166 --> 00:21:53.750
Uh… Look,
I know that you're really upset with me.

372
00:21:53.833 --> 00:21:55.000
Just get to the point.

373
00:21:55.625 --> 00:21:57.125
I just wanted to say that I--

374
00:21:57.208 --> 00:21:58.375
What do you want to say?

375
00:22:00.958 --> 00:22:02.125
I'm on my way to Korea.

376
00:22:02.208 --> 00:22:03.500
<i>What's the point now?</i>

377
00:22:03.583 --> 00:22:05.250
You humiliated you dad
when he came to see you.

378
00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:07.541
Dad came to see me?

379
00:22:07.625 --> 00:22:09.208
[thunder rumbling]

380
00:22:09.791 --> 00:22:11.208
<i>You insulted him</i>

381
00:22:11.291 --> 00:22:13.208
and then you had the audacity
to take money from him?

382
00:22:13.291 --> 00:22:14.625
Mom, what are you talking about?

383
00:22:19.458 --> 00:22:21.291
Sir, what are you doing here?
What the hell do you want?

384
00:22:21.375 --> 00:22:23.083
She had applied for a loan at the bank.

385
00:22:23.166 --> 00:22:25.000
I have got the money
and I don't want her money.

386
00:22:25.083 --> 00:22:26.041
Just call her, I'll give it to her.

387
00:22:26.125 --> 00:22:27.666
She doesn't want to see you!

388
00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:29.416
Don't create a scene here.
For God's sake, just leave.

389
00:22:34.041 --> 00:22:36.541
Listen, there's no need
to tell her all this.

390
00:22:37.083 --> 00:22:38.875
<i>She needs to know what happened.</i>

391
00:22:42.208 --> 00:22:43.541
[thunder rumbling]

392
00:22:47.083 --> 00:22:49.125
Sir, why the hell are you still here?

393
00:22:49.208 --> 00:22:51.125
I don't have time for this.
Tell her to come out and take the money.

394
00:22:51.833 --> 00:22:55.041
I told her that you're here,
but she doesn't want to come and see you.

395
00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:10.500
It's her money, give it to her.

396
00:23:12.666 --> 00:23:14.916
[Shenbagam's mom] <i>You really think</i>
<i>you got a loan from the bank?</i>

397
00:23:15.458 --> 00:23:16.708
<i>Who would give you a loan?</i>

398
00:23:16.791 --> 00:23:19.916
<i>That was his own money.</i>
<i>All his life savings.</i>

399
00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.916
[pilot] <i>We are lining up on the runway.</i>

400
00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.375
<i>Cabin crew,</i>
<i>please take your seats for take-off.</i>

401
00:23:24.458 --> 00:23:26.375
<i>Please ensure your seatbelts are fastened…</i>

402
00:23:26.458 --> 00:23:28.083
Oh, I'll just call you back.

403
00:23:28.791 --> 00:23:31.958
[dialing]

404
00:23:32.041 --> 00:23:33.708
[sighs]

405
00:23:36.125 --> 00:23:38.083
[cell phone vibrating]

406
00:23:40.916 --> 00:23:44.250
[pilot] <i>Our flying time to Mumbai</i>
<i>is one hour and forty minutes.</i>

407
00:23:47.625 --> 00:23:50.000
<i>The weather in Mumbai is clear and sunny.</i>

408
00:23:57.791 --> 00:24:00.583
[operator] <i>The number you are calling</i>
<i>is either switched off</i>

409
00:24:00.666 --> 00:24:02.875
<i>or not reachable at the moment.</i>

410
00:24:02.958 --> 00:24:04.333
<i>Please try later.</i>

411
00:24:06.333 --> 00:24:08.166
[pilot] <i>Thank you</i>
<i>for choosing to fly with us today.</i>

412
00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:09.833
<i>Enjoy the flight.</i>

413
00:24:11.708 --> 00:24:14.125
And my father's debts,
they're piling up on my head.

414
00:24:14.208 --> 00:24:15.333
Just give me some time.

415
00:24:15.416 --> 00:24:16.833
Remember I told you about
a friend in Mumbai?

416
00:24:16.916 --> 00:24:18.500
I've been planning on starting
a business with him.

417
00:24:18.583 --> 00:24:20.125
Tell her to come out
and take the money from me now.

418
00:24:20.208 --> 00:24:21.333
She doesn't want to see you!

419
00:24:21.416 --> 00:24:23.166
You don't need to worry about the money.
I'll manage.

420
00:24:23.250 --> 00:24:26.375
Just come with me, but you can't ask
where I'm taking you, you understand?

421
00:24:26.458 --> 00:24:28.250
You will never question me again,
do you get it?

422
00:24:31.166 --> 00:24:33.083
[Shenbagam's dad] <i>He is going to</i>
<i>abandon you one day.</i>

423
00:24:33.166 --> 00:24:34.125
<i>It's only a matter of time.</i>

424
00:25:19.125 --> 00:25:21.000
Good evening, ma'am. What's your name?

425
00:25:21.083 --> 00:25:23.166
Uh, Shenbagam.

426
00:25:23.708 --> 00:25:24.958
What are you doing in Korea?

427
00:25:25.666 --> 00:25:30.541
Well, I'm here for work,
uh, for 12 months.

428
00:25:30.625 --> 00:25:32.875
And this… this is the visa.

429
00:25:41.208 --> 00:25:42.375
[officer in Korean] Next.

430
00:25:44.166 --> 00:25:46.416
[Shenbagam]
<i>My first ever international trip.</i>

431
00:25:46.500 --> 00:25:48.083
<i>Seoul, Korea.</i>

432
00:25:48.166 --> 00:25:50.375
<i>I used to dream about coming here.</i>

433
00:25:50.458 --> 00:25:52.708
<i>I thought I'd be happy when I come here,</i>

434
00:25:52.791 --> 00:25:55.083
<i>but today, I have no reason to be happy.</i>

435
00:26:47.833 --> 00:26:49.583
-[performer in Korean] Ready?
-[crowd] Yeah.

436
00:26:51.208 --> 00:26:53.333
{\an8}Wow! That's so cool.

437
00:27:02.500 --> 00:27:06.541
[shivering]

438
00:27:07.958 --> 00:27:08.916
Wow!

439
00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.458
Wow! Thank you so much.

440
00:27:19.083 --> 00:27:20.333
[gasps]

441
00:27:45.083 --> 00:27:46.583
[effort grunts]

442
00:27:46.666 --> 00:27:49.208
Sir, Hotel Niagara?

443
00:27:49.708 --> 00:27:51.083
Uh, Hotel Niagara?

444
00:27:51.625 --> 00:27:52.500
[in Korean] Sorry, I don't know.

445
00:27:53.125 --> 00:27:54.916
[in English] Hotel Niagara. Can you?

446
00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:56.750
Booked, booked, already booked.

447
00:27:56.833 --> 00:27:58.208
Hotel Niagara?

448
00:27:58.750 --> 00:28:00.583
-Okay, okay.
-[effort grunts]

449
00:28:40.541 --> 00:28:41.750
[effort grunts]

450
00:28:48.833 --> 00:28:49.708
Hello.

451
00:28:55.041 --> 00:28:56.291
Passport.

452
00:29:14.291 --> 00:29:15.208
[cell phone beeps]

453
00:29:19.958 --> 00:29:23.125
[Mani] <i>What I did was wrong</i>
<i>and I know that.</i>

454
00:29:23.208 --> 00:29:24.916
<i>I had no other choice.</i>

455
00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:26.500
<i>I wish it wasn't like this.</i>

456
00:29:26.583 --> 00:29:29.208
<i>I did what I did</i>
<i>because I thought it's best for you.</i>

457
00:29:29.291 --> 00:29:31.750
<i>And whatever happened,</i>
<i>you're in Korea now.</i>

458
00:29:32.458 --> 00:29:34.666
<i>Otherwise,</i>
<i>your dream would never have come true.</i>

459
00:29:34.750 --> 00:29:37.583
<i>I am not in a position to think</i>
<i>whether I was right or wrong…</i>

460
00:29:38.375 --> 00:29:42.208
<i>but you're finally in Korea</i>
<i>and that is all that matters.</i>

461
00:29:42.291 --> 00:29:44.916
<i>Hope you have a good life.</i>
<i>Wish you all the best.</i>

462
00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:46.416
-[scoffs]
-[cell phone thuds]

463
00:30:28.333 --> 00:30:30.208
[in Korean] Excuse me,
do you not see a queue?

464
00:30:30.291 --> 00:30:31.333
Please stand at the back of the queue.

465
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:41.541
[thunder rumbling]

466
00:30:46.125 --> 00:30:47.333
[device beeps]

467
00:30:49.125 --> 00:30:50.083
[device beeps]

468
00:30:52.375 --> 00:30:53.791
Scan your bus card here, please.

469
00:30:53.875 --> 00:30:54.875
[in English] Um, money?

470
00:30:54.958 --> 00:30:56.083
No.

471
00:30:56.166 --> 00:30:58.083
[in Korean] Scan your bus card here
or de-board the bus, please.

472
00:31:10.666 --> 00:31:12.666
[train horn blowing]

473
00:31:37.208 --> 00:31:38.750
[rain pattering]

474
00:31:58.125 --> 00:31:59.250
-[distant siren wailing]
-[clicks tongue]

475
00:32:23.291 --> 00:32:24.750
[door bell jingling]

476
00:32:24.833 --> 00:32:26.416
[in Korean] Welcome!

477
00:32:27.583 --> 00:32:29.250
{\an8}[in English] Uh, one soju.

478
00:32:29.333 --> 00:32:30.750
{\an8}Ah, one soju?

479
00:32:30.833 --> 00:32:34.208
{\an8}No! Somaek, Somaek. Two.

480
00:32:57.125 --> 00:32:58.000
[grunts]

481
00:33:02.916 --> 00:33:04.958
-[grunts]
-[line ringing]

482
00:33:06.125 --> 00:33:08.083
Mani, come on, answer the call.

483
00:33:08.625 --> 00:33:10.708
Answer the call. I want to talk to you.

484
00:33:11.708 --> 00:33:12.833
Pick up the call!

485
00:33:12.916 --> 00:33:15.041
{\an8}[line ringing]

486
00:33:15.125 --> 00:33:16.500
[line disconnects]

487
00:33:18.458 --> 00:33:19.375
Call me!

488
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:22.250
I want to talk to you right now. Call me!

489
00:33:22.333 --> 00:33:25.291
If you don't call me now,
I will never speak to you again.

490
00:33:25.375 --> 00:33:26.375
Answer the call!

491
00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:31.000
[sighs, grunts]

492
00:33:37.875 --> 00:33:39.666
[wearily] Answer my call.

493
00:33:42.875 --> 00:33:44.916
[sobs softly] Please.

494
00:33:46.625 --> 00:33:47.708
[sniffles]

495
00:34:09.416 --> 00:34:10.416
Hmm?

496
00:34:31.666 --> 00:34:32.541
-[grunts]
-[man] Oh.

497
00:34:34.583 --> 00:34:38.416
[couple quarreling]

498
00:34:38.500 --> 00:34:39.750
[in Korean] Stop!

499
00:34:39.833 --> 00:34:42.166
[both continue quarreling]

500
00:34:42.250 --> 00:34:43.375
-[man] Uh…
-[gasps]

501
00:34:46.375 --> 00:34:47.958
[in English]
I left everything behind for you.

502
00:34:48.708 --> 00:34:50.291
How dare you break my trust like this?

503
00:34:50.875 --> 00:34:51.708
Huh?

504
00:34:51.791 --> 00:34:54.625
{\an8}We have been together for eight years
and you just abandoned me?

505
00:34:54.708 --> 00:34:56.416
{\an8}How could you do this? [sobs]

506
00:34:56.500 --> 00:34:57.458
{\an8}[sniffles]

507
00:34:57.541 --> 00:34:58.791
{\an8}You're a cheat.

508
00:34:59.333 --> 00:35:00.416
What? What?

509
00:35:01.916 --> 00:35:02.916
Get lost!

510
00:35:03.708 --> 00:35:04.708
Come on.

511
00:35:08.416 --> 00:35:09.541
Sit down.

512
00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:14.000
He asked you to come along
so you just went along? Are you stupid?

513
00:35:15.333 --> 00:35:17.208
Serves you right. You deserve it.

514
00:35:18.458 --> 00:35:20.833
You hurt your parents
and that is why he hurt you.

515
00:35:21.416 --> 00:35:22.500
Karma! Karma!

516
00:35:24.875 --> 00:35:25.916
Wipe your tears.

517
00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:27.041
Hmm?

518
00:35:27.625 --> 00:35:29.208
[clicks tongue] Stop crying.

519
00:35:30.791 --> 00:35:31.750
[sighs]

520
00:35:34.125 --> 00:35:38.625
[cell phone ringing]

521
00:35:38.708 --> 00:35:40.125
[clicks tongue] Not this idiot.

522
00:35:42.625 --> 00:35:43.541
What?

523
00:35:43.625 --> 00:35:45.750
Didn't I tell you
the moment I saw that guy

524
00:35:45.833 --> 00:35:46.666
that he's good for nothing?

525
00:35:46.750 --> 00:35:47.750
<i>But you didn't listen.</i>

526
00:35:47.833 --> 00:35:50.625
You did what you always wanted to do.
Now pack your bags and come back.

527
00:35:50.708 --> 00:35:53.291
I can't. Why should I?
What will do there? Tell me.

528
00:35:53.375 --> 00:35:55.083
"Oh, Dad, please forgive me."

529
00:35:55.166 --> 00:35:56.583
You want me to come and apologize to him?

530
00:35:56.666 --> 00:35:58.416
<i>Why not?</i>
<i>You don't know anyone in that country.</i>

531
00:35:58.500 --> 00:35:59.375
<i>What the hell are you gonna do?</i>

532
00:35:59.458 --> 00:36:00.791
I will figure it out.

533
00:36:01.333 --> 00:36:05.458
This is my favorite country.
I can live here. Just leave me alone.

534
00:36:07.333 --> 00:36:08.833
-Why are you still here?
-Hmm?

535
00:36:08.916 --> 00:36:09.875
He's left already.

536
00:36:09.958 --> 00:36:10.791
Hmm?

537
00:36:10.875 --> 00:36:12.458
[officers singing in Korean]
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

538
00:36:12.541 --> 00:36:16.625
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you</i>
<i>Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

539
00:36:16.708 --> 00:36:17.750
[all cheering]

540
00:36:17.833 --> 00:36:19.958
[hiccupping]

541
00:36:20.958 --> 00:36:22.041
[sighs]

542
00:36:23.541 --> 00:36:24.500
[sighs]

543
00:36:36.875 --> 00:36:38.666
[woman in Korean] It's done.

544
00:36:47.708 --> 00:36:48.750
[in English] Oh, no.

545
00:36:50.125 --> 00:36:51.791
I forgot to pay for the drinks.

546
00:36:56.583 --> 00:36:58.291
[grunts, sighs]

547
00:36:58.375 --> 00:36:59.916
[officer in Korean] Oh, who bought this?

548
00:37:01.833 --> 00:37:03.000
[imperceptible conversation]

549
00:37:03.083 --> 00:37:04.083
[sighs]

550
00:37:06.500 --> 00:37:07.750
[in Korean] No, give it to her first.

551
00:37:07.833 --> 00:37:09.458
[woman laughing]

552
00:37:09.541 --> 00:37:10.458
Okay, okay, okay, here.

553
00:37:16.250 --> 00:37:17.416
Tell me something.

554
00:37:17.500 --> 00:37:20.958
Who the hell goes around town
slapping people randomly?

555
00:37:21.041 --> 00:37:23.708
Don't you know that it's illegal, huh?

556
00:37:23.791 --> 00:37:24.791
[in English] I don't get it.

557
00:37:26.291 --> 00:37:27.458
Why am I here?

558
00:37:28.083 --> 00:37:30.208
For drinking or hitting someone?

559
00:37:30.291 --> 00:37:33.041
[in Korean] Someone's here
and they're asking about this woman.

560
00:37:33.125 --> 00:37:34.333
-Really?
-Yes.

561
00:37:34.416 --> 00:37:35.958
[in English] What is going on?

562
00:37:36.041 --> 00:37:37.333
[in Korean] How can I help you?

563
00:37:37.416 --> 00:37:41.250
Is there a foreign lady
who was brought in here?

564
00:37:41.333 --> 00:37:42.583
About this tall?

565
00:37:42.666 --> 00:37:44.250
You her guardian?

566
00:37:44.333 --> 00:37:45.291
Yeah, sure.

567
00:37:45.375 --> 00:37:46.541
[sniffles]

568
00:37:53.125 --> 00:37:55.958
So, you're telling me that
this man was hitting his girlfriend?

569
00:37:56.041 --> 00:37:58.208
-Yeah, yeah.
-And this woman slapped the guy

570
00:37:58.291 --> 00:37:59.500
to save her?

571
00:37:59.583 --> 00:38:01.708
Sorry for all the trouble.

572
00:38:01.791 --> 00:38:02.833
[officer] Bring her.

573
00:38:08.875 --> 00:38:10.666
Here you go. Sign on the dotted line.

574
00:38:10.750 --> 00:38:12.375
-Get this signed and she can leave.
-[in English] Sign, sign.

575
00:38:12.458 --> 00:38:14.208
Who are you?

576
00:38:14.291 --> 00:38:16.291
I should sign because you are saying so?

577
00:38:16.375 --> 00:38:17.583
[sighs]

578
00:38:22.541 --> 00:38:25.708
"If you sign, you can leave.

579
00:38:25.791 --> 00:38:30.125
If you don't sign,
you will stay here, I will go."

580
00:38:31.333 --> 00:38:33.875
I'm ready to sign.
Where… Where do I sign? Where?

581
00:38:40.625 --> 00:38:42.958
-[in Korean] You can take her now.
-Thank you, thank you, sir.

582
00:38:43.041 --> 00:38:44.708
Let's go.

583
00:38:45.666 --> 00:38:46.833
Thank you.

584
00:38:49.291 --> 00:38:52.041
[in English] If a man had harassed
a woman like this

585
00:38:52.125 --> 00:38:54.208
on the side of the road in my village,

586
00:38:54.291 --> 00:38:56.666
I would've slapped him across his face.

587
00:38:56.750 --> 00:38:58.541
[in Korean]
What in the world is she saying?

588
00:38:58.625 --> 00:38:59.625
[scoffs]

589
00:39:00.750 --> 00:39:02.625
-It sounds like she's cursing at me.
-Nothing at all, sir.

590
00:39:02.708 --> 00:39:05.041
Just that she is grateful. Thank you.

591
00:39:05.125 --> 00:39:06.833
Thank you. Thank you.

592
00:39:09.291 --> 00:39:10.125
[sighs]

593
00:39:11.416 --> 00:39:12.333
{\an8}[in English] Who are you?

594
00:39:13.416 --> 00:39:14.958
I am Heo Jun-Jae.

595
00:39:18.416 --> 00:39:20.416
Heo Jun-Jae what? Hey, you!

596
00:39:21.250 --> 00:39:22.250
Why did you help me?

597
00:39:22.333 --> 00:39:24.875
Who are you? What are you doing in Korea?

598
00:39:25.958 --> 00:39:27.666
-I am Shenbagam.
-Mmm.

599
00:39:27.750 --> 00:39:30.500
I am here for a job
at a big hotel, actually.

600
00:39:30.583 --> 00:39:32.500
-Hmm.
-Azira Hospitality.

601
00:39:32.583 --> 00:39:33.833
-Hmm.
-Mapo-gu area.

602
00:39:33.916 --> 00:39:35.666
[clicks tongue] Be safe in Korea.

603
00:39:35.750 --> 00:39:36.625
I'm okay.

604
00:39:40.291 --> 00:39:41.375
[in Korean] Thank you.

605
00:39:52.208 --> 00:39:54.000
[in English] Hey! Who the hell are you?

606
00:39:54.083 --> 00:39:56.291
I see what you're doing here.
Why are you following me?

607
00:39:57.333 --> 00:39:59.666
Do you know who I am? Huh?
Why are you following me?

608
00:39:59.750 --> 00:40:00.708
What the hell do you want from me?

609
00:40:00.791 --> 00:40:02.458
No, no, listen.

610
00:40:02.541 --> 00:40:03.583
What is it? Speak up.

611
00:40:03.666 --> 00:40:04.500
[in Korean] You see that?

612
00:40:05.333 --> 00:40:06.708
[in English] My mom's house.

613
00:40:06.791 --> 00:40:08.208
[in Korean] My mother lives there.

614
00:40:09.291 --> 00:40:11.375
I come for kimchi.

615
00:40:11.458 --> 00:40:12.833
[in Korean] Green onion kimchi.

616
00:40:12.916 --> 00:40:14.833
[in English] Okay, so, I go.

617
00:40:16.833 --> 00:40:19.416
-[clicks tongue]
-Oh! Wait, wait.

618
00:40:20.750 --> 00:40:21.625
What is it?

619
00:40:23.375 --> 00:40:26.875
Here you go. Your soju bill.

620
00:40:27.750 --> 00:40:29.833
Next time you that you drink soju,

621
00:40:29.916 --> 00:40:31.041
[in Korean] make the payment.

622
00:40:31.125 --> 00:40:32.750
[in English] Must pay, huh?

623
00:40:32.833 --> 00:40:34.125
This time I paid.

624
00:40:34.833 --> 00:40:37.416
You don't pay this. This is illegal.

625
00:40:38.125 --> 00:40:40.458
Okay? Bye.

626
00:41:02.375 --> 00:41:03.625
[store assistant in Korean] Thank you.

627
00:41:04.166 --> 00:41:05.875
-[in English] Card?
-What?

628
00:41:06.375 --> 00:41:07.875
Um, bus card?

629
00:41:09.541 --> 00:41:10.375
Ah, okay.

630
00:41:48.583 --> 00:41:50.583
Where's this company? Can you help me?

631
00:41:50.666 --> 00:41:52.833
Uh, is this the same?

632
00:41:52.916 --> 00:41:54.666
[in Korean] Yeah, it's right over there.

633
00:41:54.750 --> 00:41:55.750
Uh…

634
00:41:56.583 --> 00:41:58.666
{\an8}[in English] See the logo. Where is it?

635
00:41:59.291 --> 00:42:00.291
[gasps]

636
00:42:00.958 --> 00:42:02.041
Same.

637
00:42:03.041 --> 00:42:06.500
Not this. It's supposed to be a big hotel.
This one is small.

638
00:42:07.583 --> 00:42:09.041
-[gasps]
-Same.

639
00:42:09.125 --> 00:42:10.208
Same!

640
00:42:21.416 --> 00:42:23.000
[teasing laugh]

641
00:42:23.083 --> 00:42:25.000
[whooping]

642
00:42:25.083 --> 00:42:27.458
I know it's fake letter.

643
00:42:27.541 --> 00:42:28.750
If I tell you yesterday,

644
00:42:28.833 --> 00:42:30.583
I told you, you don't believe me.

645
00:42:31.083 --> 00:42:32.958
[in Korean] Look at this.
It's a fake company.

646
00:42:33.958 --> 00:42:37.833
Fake letter. This is a scam.

647
00:42:38.750 --> 00:42:40.208
Scam. Scam.

648
00:42:45.166 --> 00:42:46.333
You got scammed.

649
00:42:46.416 --> 00:42:49.208
Don't laugh at me!
I came here because of that letter.

650
00:42:49.291 --> 00:42:51.583
There's no way I can go back home now.

651
00:42:51.666 --> 00:42:54.291
I need a job, I need the money
and I… [sighs]

652
00:42:56.000 --> 00:42:57.500
I need a job.

653
00:42:57.583 --> 00:42:59.375
I need money, cash.

654
00:43:00.125 --> 00:43:02.125
Please, please help me.

655
00:43:03.375 --> 00:43:04.625
In here,

656
00:43:04.708 --> 00:43:07.833
Koreans themselves struggle find job.

657
00:43:07.916 --> 00:43:10.333
Why do you think they would hire
Indians here?

658
00:43:12.041 --> 00:43:13.083
[clicks tongue]

659
00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:16.041
Okay, forget about it.

660
00:43:17.208 --> 00:43:18.250
Do you have a job?

661
00:43:18.333 --> 00:43:21.375
I told you. Vlog. YouTube.

662
00:43:21.458 --> 00:43:24.041
Food, travel.

663
00:43:24.125 --> 00:43:26.125
'Travel with Jun-Jae.'

664
00:43:26.208 --> 00:43:29.958
-Everyone nowadays is a vlogger.
-I have 3,000 subscribers.

665
00:43:30.041 --> 00:43:31.041
Hmm.

666
00:43:32.416 --> 00:43:34.458
I want a real job.

667
00:43:34.541 --> 00:43:37.291
I need to get paid. You understand?

668
00:43:37.375 --> 00:43:39.083
[clicks tongue, sighs]

669
00:43:48.666 --> 00:43:51.333
-See? Job, job, job.
-Jobs?

670
00:43:59.416 --> 00:44:03.166
Um, uh, what do these… What do these say?

671
00:44:03.250 --> 00:44:05.000
Can you help me?

672
00:44:05.083 --> 00:44:06.166
This one, this one.

673
00:44:06.250 --> 00:44:07.750
Driver. Okay?

674
00:44:07.833 --> 00:44:09.875
I don't have a licence.

675
00:44:09.958 --> 00:44:11.250
Pets?

676
00:44:11.333 --> 00:44:14.000
Hmm. It's okay. Give it to me. I will try.

677
00:44:14.083 --> 00:44:16.541
Oh. Oh! This one, tour guide.

678
00:44:16.625 --> 00:44:18.000
Who is going to guide me?

679
00:44:18.083 --> 00:44:18.958
[imitates sweeping]

680
00:44:19.041 --> 00:44:20.041
-Cleaner?
-No.

681
00:44:20.125 --> 00:44:21.333
Gift packing.

682
00:44:21.416 --> 00:44:22.750
Okay, give!

683
00:44:23.458 --> 00:44:24.625
I'll come with you.

684
00:44:25.500 --> 00:44:26.916
No need.

685
00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:29.000
I-- I will handle it.

686
00:44:29.083 --> 00:44:31.083
It's okay. I'll go on my own.

687
00:44:31.583 --> 00:44:32.708
Wait.

688
00:44:38.875 --> 00:44:41.416
[speaking Korean]

689
00:44:42.833 --> 00:44:44.166
[automated voice in English]
<i>Take this with you.</i>

690
00:44:44.250 --> 00:44:46.166
<i>If you have this, it will help you.</i>

691
00:44:47.625 --> 00:44:48.750
What is this?

692
00:44:48.833 --> 00:44:50.000
Translator.

693
00:44:51.083 --> 00:44:52.250
Thank you.

694
00:44:52.333 --> 00:44:53.916
[automated voice speaking Korean]

695
00:44:55.250 --> 00:44:56.250
[chuckles]

696
00:44:56.333 --> 00:44:58.166
Whatever I say,
will you translate it correctly?

697
00:44:58.250 --> 00:45:00.041
I'm really, really hungry.

698
00:45:00.125 --> 00:45:01.375
[automated voice speaking Korean]

699
00:45:01.458 --> 00:45:03.000
I need a job right now!

700
00:45:03.083 --> 00:45:05.083
[automated voice speaking Korean]

701
00:45:13.291 --> 00:45:16.083
[speaking Korean]

702
00:45:23.041 --> 00:45:24.250
[gasps]

703
00:45:24.333 --> 00:45:25.916
Oh, sorry!

704
00:45:32.375 --> 00:45:34.250
[Indian pop music playing]

705
00:45:43.375 --> 00:45:44.416
You have to clean it.

706
00:45:44.500 --> 00:45:46.500
Oh, no, no. No.

707
00:45:54.041 --> 00:45:56.083
Don't worry, this is my house.

708
00:47:13.125 --> 00:47:17.458
[playing traditional
Indian music on violin]

709
00:47:52.833 --> 00:47:55.166
Hi. Hi, Shenba!

710
00:47:55.916 --> 00:47:57.166
Job, job.

711
00:47:58.875 --> 00:48:01.916
Ten minutes, come down. I'll pick you up.

712
00:48:05.500 --> 00:48:06.958
Hello? Where are we going?

713
00:48:07.041 --> 00:48:08.125
A job.

714
00:48:08.208 --> 00:48:11.041
-Huh?
-Job. Job for you.

715
00:48:11.125 --> 00:48:12.750
Mmm, if we ever get there on time.

716
00:48:12.833 --> 00:48:14.916
-People are walking faster than us.
-What?

717
00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:17.250
-Nothing, nothing. Keep going!
-Oh!

718
00:48:18.916 --> 00:48:20.583
[in Korean]
Don't worry, I'll be there soon.

719
00:48:20.666 --> 00:48:22.125
[in English] Okay.

720
00:48:22.916 --> 00:48:24.666
[in Korean] How are you doing?

721
00:48:24.750 --> 00:48:28.250
I'm fine, thank you. I had spoke to you
on the phone. I'm Heo Jun-Jae,

722
00:48:28.333 --> 00:48:29.833
and her name is Shenba.

723
00:48:31.166 --> 00:48:33.083
[in English] Hi, I am Hung Swa.

724
00:48:33.166 --> 00:48:35.041
Oh, nice to meet you.

725
00:48:35.125 --> 00:48:37.041
My mom is sick.

726
00:48:37.125 --> 00:48:40.791
She can't move, walk or talk.
Only gestures.

727
00:48:40.875 --> 00:48:43.583
She is… You understand?

728
00:48:43.666 --> 00:48:44.958
Yes, I understand.

729
00:48:45.041 --> 00:48:47.166
Just do your best to take care of her.

730
00:48:47.250 --> 00:48:49.125
-Oh, okay.
-That would be… enough.

731
00:48:49.208 --> 00:48:53.083
Okay, uh, but… what's the job?

732
00:48:53.166 --> 00:48:57.458
Caretaker. Ah, like, maid.

733
00:48:58.750 --> 00:48:59.791
A maid?

734
00:48:59.875 --> 00:49:02.833
Maid. Clean, clean, clean.

735
00:49:02.916 --> 00:49:04.041
Oh.

736
00:49:04.541 --> 00:49:06.666
<i>He wants me to be a housemaid?</i>

737
00:49:06.750 --> 00:49:08.875
<i>I've never ever done chores</i>
<i>in my own house.</i>

738
00:49:08.958 --> 00:49:10.375
You okay?

739
00:49:10.458 --> 00:49:11.541
Sure, sir!

740
00:49:11.625 --> 00:49:13.250
It will do it. I will take care of her.

741
00:49:13.333 --> 00:49:16.125
At my own place,
I do all the work, you know.

742
00:49:16.208 --> 00:49:17.833
This is my address.

743
00:49:17.916 --> 00:49:21.250
-Oh.
-Morning, 10:00 a.m., come to my home.

744
00:49:21.333 --> 00:49:22.958
Thank you.

745
00:49:23.041 --> 00:49:25.708
[both in Korean] Thank you so much.
Thank you so much.

746
00:49:25.791 --> 00:49:27.208
Don't be late.

747
00:49:43.500 --> 00:49:44.708
Omma.

748
00:49:45.625 --> 00:49:46.666
Omma?

749
00:49:50.791 --> 00:49:53.875
{\an8}[in Korean]
I've found so many caretakers for you.

750
00:49:53.958 --> 00:49:57.083
{\an8}But I don't understand
why they all keep quitting.

751
00:49:57.166 --> 00:50:00.958
I've managed to find another person,
but she can't speak Korean.

752
00:50:01.041 --> 00:50:02.750
Try to work it out with her please.

753
00:50:07.291 --> 00:50:08.708
[in English] Shenba.

754
00:50:08.791 --> 00:50:10.375
Calling you.

755
00:50:20.666 --> 00:50:22.875
She is my mother. Omma.

756
00:50:22.958 --> 00:50:27.875
Always keep her clean, feed her on time,
and take care of her.

757
00:50:27.958 --> 00:50:29.208
Okay, sir. Okay.

758
00:50:29.291 --> 00:50:32.166
Keeping her clean is not your only job.

759
00:50:32.833 --> 00:50:35.666
Keep the kitchen and floor clean.

760
00:50:35.750 --> 00:50:38.500
We will come around eight o'clock.

761
00:50:38.583 --> 00:50:42.791
Before that, do the work and leave.

762
00:50:43.458 --> 00:50:44.333
Okay.

763
00:51:23.666 --> 00:51:25.333
[clatter in distance]

764
00:51:25.416 --> 00:51:26.458
[gasps]

765
00:52:02.208 --> 00:52:04.875
-Kitchen, floor clean?
-Yeah.

766
00:52:04.958 --> 00:52:07.333
-Omma is fine?
-Yeah, yeah, she's fine.

767
00:52:07.416 --> 00:52:09.875
Okay, you can leave.
Come tomorrow morning.

768
00:52:53.208 --> 00:52:55.000
-[clatter in distance]
-[gasps]

769
00:53:18.291 --> 00:53:19.416
[gasps]

770
00:53:28.125 --> 00:53:28.958
[gasps]

771
00:53:29.041 --> 00:53:32.875
[distorted metal guitar playing]

772
00:53:38.458 --> 00:53:39.750
[heavy drumbeat playing]

773
00:54:01.750 --> 00:54:02.791
Stop!

774
00:54:04.375 --> 00:54:06.500
Stop making noise.

775
00:54:20.875 --> 00:54:22.500
[in Korean] Hey. Let's go.

776
00:54:22.583 --> 00:54:23.500
Sure.

777
00:54:23.583 --> 00:54:24.916
She's scary.

778
00:54:25.000 --> 00:54:26.791
-[cymbal crashes]
-[both] Oh!

779
00:54:34.666 --> 00:54:35.833
Muruga.

780
00:54:39.500 --> 00:54:40.500
I've got this.

781
00:55:08.000 --> 00:55:09.208
Food.

782
00:55:34.000 --> 00:55:34.875
[gasps]

783
00:55:48.791 --> 00:55:51.500
[in Korean] Don't ask me why I pretend
to be sick, because it's personal.

784
00:55:51.583 --> 00:55:54.125
[in English] Ah, one minute.

785
00:56:01.416 --> 00:56:03.750
[in Korean] Don't ask me why I pretend
to be sick, because it's personal.

786
00:56:03.833 --> 00:56:06.416
[automated voice in English]
<i>Don't ask me why I pretend to be sick,</i>

787
00:56:06.500 --> 00:56:08.416
<i>because it's personal.</i>

788
00:56:08.500 --> 00:56:10.750
<i>If you don't want</i>
<i>to be fired from this job,</i>

789
00:56:10.833 --> 00:56:12.416
<i>you must do as I say.</i>

790
00:56:12.500 --> 00:56:15.708
<i>Usually it takes ten days</i>
<i>for my caretaker to find out,</i>

791
00:56:15.791 --> 00:56:17.750
<i>but you figured it out in three days.</i>

792
00:56:17.833 --> 00:56:20.708
<i>I must say, you are way smarter</i>
<i>than you look.</i>

793
00:56:20.791 --> 00:56:23.041
<i>You will not tell anyone about this.</i>

794
00:56:23.125 --> 00:56:24.916
<i>You must keep your mouth shut.</i>

795
00:56:25.000 --> 00:56:26.541
<i>Open your bag.</i>

796
00:56:28.125 --> 00:56:29.625
My bag?

797
00:56:29.708 --> 00:56:31.375
[in Korean] Your bag!

798
00:56:40.291 --> 00:56:41.833
[mother speaking Korean]

799
00:56:41.916 --> 00:56:43.791
[automated voice in English]
<i>This is my son's watch.</i>

800
00:56:44.625 --> 00:56:46.750
<i>If you ever tell anyone about me,</i>

801
00:56:47.416 --> 00:56:50.041
<i>I will tell everyone that you stole it.</i>

802
00:56:50.125 --> 00:56:52.583
<i>And then I'll get you fired.</i>

803
00:56:52.666 --> 00:56:54.250
<i>You get that?</i>

804
00:56:54.333 --> 00:56:55.458
Me?

805
00:56:57.500 --> 00:56:58.750
Now…

806
00:57:01.125 --> 00:57:02.500
good girl.

807
00:57:03.958 --> 00:57:05.375
Come tomorrow.

808
00:57:07.375 --> 00:57:08.458
Okay?

809
00:57:08.541 --> 00:57:09.916
Okay.

810
00:57:17.666 --> 00:57:19.958
Oh, yeah!

811
00:57:20.625 --> 00:57:21.833
[in Korean] It has been a while!

812
00:57:22.750 --> 00:57:24.166
[in English] Huh? Nice? Nice?

813
00:57:25.958 --> 00:57:27.333
Mmm, okay.

814
00:57:27.958 --> 00:57:29.166
Thalaivar style!

815
00:57:31.041 --> 00:57:32.083
Korean Sauna.

816
00:57:32.166 --> 00:57:33.916
[in Korean] For two adults please.

817
00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:38.333
[Tamil pop music playing]

818
00:57:58.041 --> 00:57:58.875
[in English] Bye.

819
00:57:59.916 --> 00:58:01.083
You enjoyed?

820
00:58:01.166 --> 00:58:02.875
I did not, you sure did.

821
00:58:03.958 --> 00:58:05.333
Come tomorrow.

822
00:58:05.416 --> 00:58:06.416
Yeah, yeah.

823
00:58:06.500 --> 00:58:08.333
-Bye!
-Bye!

824
00:58:08.416 --> 00:58:11.333
<i>♪ The sky will guide you ♪</i>

825
00:58:11.416 --> 00:58:14.208
<i>♪ As you rise up, it will hold you ♪</i>

826
00:58:14.291 --> 00:58:17.125
<i>♪ The sky will guide you ♪</i>

827
00:58:17.208 --> 00:58:23.458
<i>♪ To make you reach</i>
<i>It will stretch out its hand ♪</i>

828
00:58:32.500 --> 00:58:35.875
<i>♪ The journey is big… ♪</i>

829
00:58:40.291 --> 00:58:42.250
[Saami on phone]
<i>Yeah, we just came back from the hospital.</i>

830
00:58:42.333 --> 00:58:43.458
What did the doctor say?

831
00:58:43.541 --> 00:58:45.041
<i>Nothing much. He said everything is fine.</i>

832
00:58:45.125 --> 00:58:46.625
Listen, I know

833
00:58:46.708 --> 00:58:48.833
what my father must be thinking about me.

834
00:58:48.916 --> 00:58:50.208
<i>You want to talk to him?</i>
<i>I'll give him the phone.</i>

835
00:58:50.291 --> 00:58:52.000
Hey, no, no! Stop it, Saami.

836
00:58:52.083 --> 00:58:53.375
<i>Why don't you just talk to him?</i>

837
00:58:53.458 --> 00:58:55.750
Just let it be, Saami.
I'll talk to him when I'm ready.

838
00:58:55.833 --> 00:58:56.916
<i>How long are you going to do this?</i>

839
00:58:57.000 --> 00:58:59.833
-Listen, I'll… I'll talk to you later.
<i>-Oh, hello! Hello?</i>

840
00:58:59.916 --> 00:59:01.666
What are you looking at?

841
00:59:01.750 --> 00:59:04.166
I know you don't understand
a word I'm saying.

842
00:59:04.250 --> 00:59:08.041
When my dad used to fall sick,
I would always be by his side.

843
00:59:08.125 --> 00:59:09.750
But I'm not with him today.

844
00:59:10.625 --> 00:59:12.416
I will pay him back one day.

845
00:59:12.500 --> 00:59:14.125
And that's a promise.

846
00:59:14.708 --> 00:59:16.583
I need to make money for that, you know.

847
00:59:22.583 --> 00:59:25.208
<i>♪ To make you reach</i>
<i>It will stretch out its hand ♪</i>

848
00:59:25.291 --> 00:59:29.125
{\an8}I feel terrible for leaving my parents
behind. It's been very difficult.

849
00:59:29.208 --> 00:59:30.916
I truly miss them.

850
00:59:31.000 --> 00:59:33.875
<i>♪ The season of rain is ending ♪</i>

851
00:59:34.666 --> 00:59:35.958
<i>♪ The journey is big ♪</i>

852
00:59:36.041 --> 00:59:37.666
SOUTH GATE

853
00:59:37.750 --> 00:59:38.916
Indian Queen.

854
00:59:41.125 --> 00:59:42.083
Ah!

855
00:59:42.166 --> 00:59:45.708
<i>♪ Good things are coming to you ♪</i>

856
00:59:45.791 --> 00:59:48.708
{\an8}<i>♪ Learn to forget the past ♪</i>

857
00:59:48.791 --> 00:59:51.708
<i>♪ Start to realize your dreams ♪</i>

858
00:59:51.791 --> 00:59:52.875
<i>♪ A wing sprouts to graze the heavens… ♪</i>

859
00:59:52.958 --> 00:59:56.458
One, two, three, four, five, six.

860
00:59:56.541 --> 00:59:58.083
Six stones from India.

861
00:59:58.625 --> 01:00:04.500
<i>♪ Truly, see the joy</i>
<i>Of fulfillment in your eyes ♪</i>

862
01:00:04.583 --> 01:00:10.666
<i>♪ The sky will guide you ♪</i>

863
01:00:10.750 --> 01:00:16.833
{\an8}<i>♪ As you rise up, it will hold you ♪</i>

864
01:00:16.916 --> 01:00:22.375
<i>♪ The sky will guide you ♪</i>

865
01:00:22.458 --> 01:00:27.833
<i>♪ To make you reach</i>
<i>It will stretch out its hand ♪</i>

866
01:00:27.916 --> 01:00:31.375
[Shenba] <i>I had always dreamed of being</i>
<i>here in my favorite place one day.</i>

867
01:00:31.458 --> 01:00:34.250
<i>I'm finally here, and I'm so happy.</i>

868
01:00:34.333 --> 01:00:37.166
[in Korean]
Do you realize that I saved you?

869
01:00:37.250 --> 01:00:39.125
[in English] Ah, one minute.

870
01:00:40.166 --> 01:00:41.625
Can you repeat that?

871
01:00:41.708 --> 01:00:43.916
[in Korean]
Do you realize that I saved you?

872
01:00:44.000 --> 01:00:45.625
[automated voice in English]
<i>You haven't saved me.</i>

873
01:00:45.708 --> 01:00:47.541
-I don't understand.
<i>-In fact, I saved you.</i>

874
01:00:47.625 --> 01:00:49.958
<i>Three days after you started</i>
<i>working for us,</i>

875
01:00:50.041 --> 01:00:51.958
<i>my son wanted to replace you.</i>

876
01:00:52.041 --> 01:00:53.708
<i>But I told him not to do that.</i>

877
01:00:53.791 --> 01:00:56.000
[speaking Korean]

878
01:00:56.083 --> 01:00:58.041
[automated voice in English]
<i>So that's how I saved you.</i>

879
01:00:59.708 --> 01:01:02.208
<i>I told him I want you and nobody else.</i>

880
01:01:03.666 --> 01:01:05.041
Thank you.

881
01:01:05.666 --> 01:01:07.791
[automated voice]
<i>I have a question for you.</i>

882
01:01:08.416 --> 01:01:11.875
<i>Why didn't you tell my son</i>
<i>and his wife about me?</i>

883
01:01:11.958 --> 01:01:13.208
[laughs]

884
01:01:13.291 --> 01:01:16.083
Are you kidding? I would have lost my job.

885
01:01:16.958 --> 01:01:18.666
But more importantly,

886
01:01:19.333 --> 01:01:21.041
I really love this job.

887
01:01:21.125 --> 01:01:22.916
And I love this place too.

888
01:01:23.000 --> 01:01:24.541
I don't want to ruin what I have.

889
01:01:30.416 --> 01:01:33.708
Tell me, how did you know
that I wouldn't tell on you?

890
01:01:33.791 --> 01:01:37.500
[automated voice speaking Korean]

891
01:01:37.583 --> 01:01:38.791
Ah!

892
01:01:40.625 --> 01:01:42.083
[speaking Korean]

893
01:01:42.166 --> 01:01:43.666
[automated voice in English]
<i>The moment I saw you,</i>

894
01:01:43.750 --> 01:01:46.208
<i>I knew for a fact that I could trust you.</i>

895
01:01:46.291 --> 01:01:48.291
<i>Tell me, how did you let</i>
<i>that boy deceive you,</i>

896
01:01:48.375 --> 01:01:49.958
<i>and how did you land up here?</i>

897
01:01:50.041 --> 01:01:51.875
Same. Trust!

898
01:01:54.666 --> 01:01:57.250
But why don't you trust your own son

899
01:01:57.333 --> 01:01:58.916
and tell him the truth?

900
01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:02.791
[automated voice speaking Korean]

901
01:02:14.041 --> 01:02:16.041
[in Korean] <i>When we were younger…</i>

902
01:02:16.833 --> 01:02:18.250
[automated voice in English]
<i>When we were younger,</i>

903
01:02:18.333 --> 01:02:21.166
<i>my husband and I used to run a restaurant.</i>

904
01:02:21.250 --> 01:02:24.583
<i>We were doing really well.</i>
<i>Our children had everything.</i>

905
01:02:24.666 --> 01:02:26.208
<i>After our children grew up,</i>

906
01:02:26.291 --> 01:02:28.625
{\an8}<i>we thought that we should enjoy our lives.</i>

907
01:02:28.708 --> 01:02:32.541
{\an8}<i>Our children got married</i>
<i>and had their own children.</i>

908
01:02:32.625 --> 01:02:34.458
<i>After my husband passed away,</i>

909
01:02:34.541 --> 01:02:36.583
<i>my children shut the restaurant down</i>

910
01:02:36.666 --> 01:02:39.208
<i>and asked me</i>
<i>to take care of their children.</i>

911
01:02:39.291 --> 01:02:41.875
<i>On that date, I lost my identity.</i>

912
01:02:41.958 --> 01:02:43.708
{\an8}<i>I forgot who I was,</i>

913
01:02:43.791 --> 01:02:45.166
{\an8}<i>what I wanted in life,</i>

914
01:02:45.250 --> 01:02:47.250
{\an8}<i>and I let my dreams go.</i>

915
01:02:48.000 --> 01:02:52.375
{\an8}<i>So one day, I made the decision</i>
<i>that I will pretend to be unwell,</i>

916
01:02:52.458 --> 01:02:57.208
<i>so that they can figure out</i>
<i>how to live their lives without my help.</i>

917
01:02:57.291 --> 01:03:01.791
<i>But circumstances were such</i>
<i>that I was forced to rely on them forever.</i>

918
01:03:01.875 --> 01:03:03.583
<i>And I did not like that at all.</i>

919
01:03:03.666 --> 01:03:07.583
<i>I want to live the last days of my life</i>
<i>not being a burden on others.</i>

920
01:03:07.666 --> 01:03:11.166
<i>I want to build something</i>
<i>that I can call my own.</i>

921
01:03:18.916 --> 01:03:21.708
[Shenba] <i>Remember you said you want</i>
<i>to live the last days of your life</i>

922
01:03:21.791 --> 01:03:23.500
<i>without depending on other people?</i>

923
01:03:23.583 --> 01:03:25.666
<i>Those words keep echoing in my head.</i>

924
01:03:27.208 --> 01:03:31.291
<i>The garlic rice and garlic pickle</i>
<i>at my father's eatery were really famous.</i>

925
01:03:32.750 --> 01:03:36.125
<i>All his customers would advise him</i>
<i>to expand the space a little,</i>

926
01:03:36.208 --> 01:03:37.750
<i>so that there's more place to sit.</i>

927
01:03:37.833 --> 01:03:42.166
<i>My father wanted me to turn his eatery</i>
<i>into a fancy restaurant one day.</i>

928
01:03:42.250 --> 01:03:45.291
<i>"It's all for you, not for me,"</i>
<i>he would say.</i>

929
01:03:45.375 --> 01:03:48.958
<i>"After I'm gone, you shouldn't</i>
<i>be dependent on anyone.</i>

930
01:03:49.041 --> 01:03:52.000
<i>You should have your own business."</i>
<i>He just kept saying that.</i>

931
01:03:52.875 --> 01:03:56.333
<i>I never understood it. But now I get it.</i>

932
01:03:57.250 --> 01:04:00.083
<i>Everything my father had dreamt</i>
<i>of doing with me,</i>

933
01:04:00.166 --> 01:04:02.166
<i>I feel like I want to do that with you.</i>

934
01:04:02.958 --> 01:04:06.875
<i>Should the two of us</i>
<i>start a small restaurant together?</i>

935
01:04:08.791 --> 01:04:10.583
[in Korean] I also…

936
01:04:10.666 --> 01:04:13.041
wanted to say the same thing.

937
01:04:13.125 --> 01:04:14.625
[in English] Same idea.

938
01:04:22.208 --> 01:04:23.541
This is all I have to give.

939
01:04:24.041 --> 01:04:25.500
Take it.

940
01:04:27.958 --> 01:04:31.041
First, we need a place.

941
01:04:34.625 --> 01:04:35.875
ON SALE

942
01:04:46.541 --> 01:04:49.541
[in Korean] Ah, doesn't this look
a little expensive to you?

943
01:04:49.625 --> 01:04:52.958
We can at least check it out,
it's not going to cost anything.

944
01:04:57.916 --> 01:04:59.750
Let's go.
What are you doing there? Come on!

945
01:04:59.833 --> 01:05:00.958
Oh!

946
01:05:01.583 --> 01:05:03.166
Thank you, have a nice day!

947
01:05:03.250 --> 01:05:06.000
Ah, we will find another place.

948
01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:10.500
COMMERCIAL PROPERTY
TO LET

949
01:05:10.583 --> 01:05:12.916
We've seen a lot of properties…
hope this one works out.

950
01:05:13.000 --> 01:05:14.166
Absolutely.

951
01:05:14.250 --> 01:05:15.791
Thank you, have a nice day!

952
01:05:21.500 --> 01:05:24.458
[in English]
Why so much struggle for this? Leave it.

953
01:05:34.750 --> 01:05:36.291
I'm not doing this just for her.

954
01:05:42.291 --> 01:05:45.250
[Heo Jun-Jae in Korean] Yes?
Yes, but that place is very cramped.

955
01:05:45.333 --> 01:05:47.708
Look, show me something
which has a low deposit.

956
01:05:48.416 --> 01:05:49.666
All right.

957
01:05:51.916 --> 01:05:53.958
[in English] Everyone is rejecting.

958
01:05:54.041 --> 01:05:55.125
No space!

959
01:05:59.291 --> 01:06:00.625
[in Korean] Can I have the check now?

960
01:06:00.708 --> 01:06:04.083
You don't have to pay
any money today. It's free.

961
01:06:05.041 --> 01:06:06.250
Why is it free?

962
01:06:06.333 --> 01:06:08.833
Today is our last day here.

963
01:06:09.333 --> 01:06:12.000
On Monday, we are opening
in another location.

964
01:06:13.083 --> 01:06:16.333
Since you're our last customer,
we thought we'd treat you.

965
01:06:17.791 --> 01:06:19.958
Sir, just a minute, I'm coming.

966
01:06:20.041 --> 01:06:21.875
I found it!

967
01:06:21.958 --> 01:06:25.416
They are closing today.
They are moving to another location.

968
01:06:26.208 --> 01:06:27.625
-Isn't this place nice?
-Yes.

969
01:06:29.750 --> 01:06:30.708
[exclaims]

970
01:06:32.166 --> 01:06:33.208
{\an8}Excuse me, sir.

971
01:06:33.791 --> 01:06:34.958
{\an8}Listen.

972
01:06:35.041 --> 01:06:39.791
{\an8}We were looking for a place
to open a restaurant.

973
01:06:39.875 --> 01:06:44.583
{\an8}Can you share the contact details
of the owner, please?

974
01:06:44.666 --> 01:06:51.416
{\an8}I need to call them. Thank you very much!

975
01:06:51.916 --> 01:06:52.958
Oh, yes.

976
01:06:53.041 --> 01:06:56.791
Shenba! Shenba! Shenba!
I think we'll get this place.

977
01:06:56.875 --> 01:07:01.541
[in English] We can start restaurant here!

978
01:07:01.625 --> 01:07:05.041
[exclaiming]

979
01:07:05.125 --> 01:07:05.958
[laughs]

980
01:07:06.500 --> 01:07:07.791
[siren wailing]

981
01:07:13.958 --> 01:07:17.000
[in Korean] This is the same
police officer that arrested Shenba.

982
01:07:18.333 --> 01:07:20.125
Who is responsible here?

983
01:07:22.375 --> 01:07:24.375
[in English] Who will pay rent?

984
01:07:28.041 --> 01:07:31.625
[in Korean] I, I… I'll pay.

985
01:07:33.541 --> 01:07:34.791
I'll pay it too.

986
01:07:34.875 --> 01:07:36.625
What do you do for a living?

987
01:07:36.708 --> 01:07:41.958
I do something like this,
I make vlogs and stuff.

988
01:07:51.208 --> 01:07:54.333
[in Korean] I know you'll pay
the rent on time.

989
01:07:54.958 --> 01:07:55.791
Mmm?

990
01:07:56.625 --> 01:07:58.416
Even if you have to beat the hell
out of four people for it.

991
01:07:59.041 --> 01:08:00.833
You look like a brawler.

992
01:08:04.458 --> 01:08:05.875
She really does.

993
01:08:06.916 --> 01:08:10.458
-Thank you!
-Have a nice day!

994
01:08:12.125 --> 01:08:12.958
I think we got it.

995
01:08:13.041 --> 01:08:14.833
-Right?
-Yes.

996
01:08:14.916 --> 01:08:16.416
[exclaims]

997
01:08:16.500 --> 01:08:18.583
[clicks tongue, in English]
Hey, what is it?

998
01:08:18.666 --> 01:08:19.750
What's happening?

999
01:08:20.291 --> 01:08:21.750
-[singing in Tamil]
-[soft music playing]

1000
01:08:24.708 --> 01:08:25.750
[translator on phone] <i>You will pay</i>

1001
01:08:25.833 --> 01:08:28.333
<i>the rent even if you have</i>
<i>to beat people up to do so.</i>

1002
01:08:28.416 --> 01:08:30.375
Yeah, yeah, don't worry.
I'll do it for sure.

1003
01:08:31.208 --> 01:08:32.750
[soft music continues]

1004
01:08:48.791 --> 01:08:50.958
[in English] Shenba, let's cut the ribbon.

1005
01:08:51.625 --> 01:08:53.208
Wait, my friends are coming.

1006
01:08:53.291 --> 01:08:56.208
In entire Korea, I am your only friend.

1007
01:08:56.291 --> 01:08:59.166
Just look at that group.

1008
01:08:59.250 --> 01:09:01.916
<i>♪ Everything is gonna be all right ♪</i>

1009
01:09:02.000 --> 01:09:05.541
<i>♪ Everything is gonna be all right ♪</i>

1010
01:09:05.625 --> 01:09:08.291
[singing continues in Tamil]

1011
01:09:11.833 --> 01:09:15.500
<i>♪ Everything is gonna be all right ♪</i>

1012
01:09:15.583 --> 01:09:18.958
<i>♪ Everything is gonna be all right ♪</i>

1013
01:09:19.041 --> 01:09:21.166
[singing continues in Tamil]

1014
01:09:37.458 --> 01:09:39.666
[all in Korean] Cheers!

1015
01:09:44.208 --> 01:09:45.375
[in English] What is this?

1016
01:09:45.458 --> 01:09:49.208
<i>Makgeolli.</i> This is a traditional
Korean drink.

1017
01:09:49.916 --> 01:09:51.041
Made with rice.

1018
01:09:56.791 --> 01:09:58.208
<i>Kanji?</i>

1019
01:09:58.291 --> 01:09:59.625
Rice <i>kanji?</i>

1020
01:09:59.708 --> 01:10:01.958
<i>-Kanji.</i>
<i>-</i>[chuckles]

1021
01:10:02.041 --> 01:10:03.083
Very nice.

1022
01:10:04.125 --> 01:10:07.666
{\an8}[in English] Granny's Kitchen
is officially open!

1023
01:10:07.750 --> 01:10:09.333
[all cheering]

1024
01:10:09.416 --> 01:10:10.666
[soft music continues]

1025
01:10:19.583 --> 01:10:20.833
[in Korean] Hello!

1026
01:10:21.666 --> 01:10:24.125
Are you hiring a part-time worker?

1027
01:10:24.208 --> 01:10:27.791
Shenba. Part-time worker.

1028
01:10:31.500 --> 01:10:34.041
Kimchi fried rice is ready!

1029
01:10:34.583 --> 01:10:35.833
Here you go. Enjoy.

1030
01:10:35.916 --> 01:10:37.125
[in English] Please, sit.

1031
01:10:39.041 --> 01:10:40.208
Menu.

1032
01:10:40.291 --> 01:10:43.416
<i>♪ Everything's gonna be all right ♪</i>

1033
01:10:43.500 --> 01:10:45.583
-Would you like to pay?
-Welcome.

1034
01:10:46.416 --> 01:10:48.791
-Did the food taste good?
-Yes. It was very good.

1035
01:10:52.791 --> 01:10:54.875
-[in English] One kimchi fried rice.
-Kimchi?

1036
01:10:57.833 --> 01:10:58.916
[in Korean] We're out of kimchi.

1037
01:11:06.541 --> 01:11:09.708
This? Garlic rice? Sorry, we're out.

1038
01:11:11.791 --> 01:11:13.250
I can make some for you though.

1039
01:11:28.166 --> 01:11:29.166
I have an idea.

1040
01:11:42.833 --> 01:11:44.333
[in English] What is this?

1041
01:11:44.416 --> 01:11:46.666
[Shenba] Indo-kimchi fried rice.

1042
01:11:47.541 --> 01:11:48.833
Indo-kimchi?

1043
01:11:53.208 --> 01:11:54.125
[in Korean] So good.

1044
01:11:55.541 --> 01:11:56.500
It's really good.

1045
01:11:56.583 --> 01:11:58.041
I'll have one of those too.

1046
01:11:58.125 --> 01:12:00.500
We just got another order of that dish!

1047
01:12:00.583 --> 01:12:01.416
[gasps]

1048
01:12:09.208 --> 01:12:13.875
<i>♪ Everything's gonna be all right ♪</i>

1049
01:12:29.291 --> 01:12:30.500
[in English] May God help me.

1050
01:12:30.583 --> 01:12:31.875
Ah.

1051
01:12:31.958 --> 01:12:34.750
[in English] Shop opening video very good.

1052
01:12:34.833 --> 01:12:37.458
Uh, can you tell me how much money
do you make?

1053
01:12:37.541 --> 01:12:41.166
Honestly, very less.

1054
01:12:41.250 --> 01:12:43.291
Who will watch if you put
the same bullshit content?

1055
01:12:43.375 --> 01:12:45.416
Think of a new idea.

1056
01:12:46.500 --> 01:12:47.333
Ah.

1057
01:12:47.958 --> 01:12:49.583
Music. Music is famous.

1058
01:12:49.666 --> 01:12:51.875
Music! That's really good.

1059
01:12:51.958 --> 01:12:54.458
Everyone is doing music content.
What's new?

1060
01:12:54.541 --> 01:12:55.541
Simple.

1061
01:12:56.666 --> 01:13:00.000
Don't target your country's audience.

1062
01:13:00.083 --> 01:13:02.041
Target other countries' audience.

1063
01:13:02.125 --> 01:13:04.708
Everybody listens to Korean music.

1064
01:13:05.791 --> 01:13:09.333
A lot of people in my village
listen to Korean music.

1065
01:13:09.416 --> 01:13:12.291
A lot of people even travel to Korea
just like me.

1066
01:13:12.375 --> 01:13:15.083
Try to add Tamil lyrics
in your Korean music.

1067
01:13:15.166 --> 01:13:18.166
It's different. Come. Let's go.

1068
01:13:22.125 --> 01:13:23.416
[in English] Why are we here?

1069
01:13:24.000 --> 01:13:26.583
Um, to help make the kimchi.

1070
01:13:26.666 --> 01:13:28.458
-Help.
-Help.

1071
01:13:30.166 --> 01:13:31.333
[whispers] Ask them.

1072
01:13:32.041 --> 01:13:33.833
One minute. I'll ask.

1073
01:13:33.916 --> 01:13:36.250
Granny? Um…

1074
01:13:37.625 --> 01:13:40.541
All of them are very talented.

1075
01:13:40.625 --> 01:13:43.916
Drums, oh, he's amazing with drums.
He's too good.

1076
01:13:45.708 --> 01:13:48.250
Violin… He is… [exclaims]

1077
01:13:49.500 --> 01:13:51.333
[all humming]

1078
01:13:51.416 --> 01:13:54.833
Oh, I'm blown away, I love it.
Too good. Too good.

1079
01:13:54.916 --> 01:13:58.416
So why don't we make…

1080
01:13:59.166 --> 01:14:00.458
a band…

1081
01:14:00.541 --> 01:14:02.500
Like K-pop?

1082
01:14:04.041 --> 01:14:06.916
Only if you guys are interested.
Otherwise, no problem.

1083
01:14:08.541 --> 01:14:12.416
I think it's a great idea.
We can upload the videos on YouTube.

1084
01:14:12.500 --> 01:14:13.541
Ah.

1085
01:14:13.625 --> 01:14:17.208
I have a separate channel.
I will shoot and edit.

1086
01:14:17.291 --> 01:14:19.916
I will do everything. Heo Jun-Jae TV.

1087
01:14:21.500 --> 01:14:24.083
But we need…

1088
01:14:24.166 --> 01:14:26.125
-Practice.
-Practice.

1089
01:14:26.208 --> 01:14:28.000
We need a space to practice.

1090
01:14:28.083 --> 01:14:29.000
Is that okay?

1091
01:14:29.083 --> 01:14:29.916
-Shenba…
-Huh?

1092
01:14:32.083 --> 01:14:37.750
Seven o'clock, use this restaurant. Huh?

1093
01:14:37.833 --> 01:14:39.333
Yeah. Uh…

1094
01:14:39.833 --> 01:14:42.916
So, seven o'clock, the kitchen closes.

1095
01:14:43.541 --> 01:14:47.250
So, you can practice
after the kitchen closes.

1096
01:14:47.333 --> 01:14:49.125
[all in Korean] Thanks!

1097
01:15:01.416 --> 01:15:02.916
[cell phone ringing]

1098
01:15:03.000 --> 01:15:05.250
-Hello, Shenba.
-Hello, sir?

1099
01:15:05.333 --> 01:15:09.541
You are taking good care of my mom.
I think she seems happy.

1100
01:15:09.625 --> 01:15:11.791
Actually, me and my wife were talking.

1101
01:15:11.875 --> 01:15:15.583
We're planning to visit our kids in Busan
this weekend.

1102
01:15:16.208 --> 01:15:20.416
Would you mind staying here
with my mom just for this weekend?

1103
01:15:21.041 --> 01:15:22.958
Okay, sir, I'll take care of her.
Don't worry about her.

1104
01:15:23.041 --> 01:15:25.166
Thank you so much, Shenba.

1105
01:15:25.791 --> 01:15:26.791
[exclaims] Yes!

1106
01:15:29.708 --> 01:15:31.916
-What are you doing?
-It's for our safety.

1107
01:15:32.000 --> 01:15:32.833
Move aside.

1108
01:15:33.958 --> 01:15:34.916
Safety?

1109
01:15:36.125 --> 01:15:37.291
Safety, what?

1110
01:15:45.166 --> 01:15:46.583
-[soft music playing]
-[singing in Tamil]

1111
01:15:58.125 --> 01:16:01.083
Listen, can you guess where Mani
is right now?

1112
01:16:01.166 --> 01:16:02.541
He's in jail.

1113
01:16:02.625 --> 01:16:05.250
Remember the guy who he went to
after betraying your trust?

1114
01:16:05.333 --> 01:16:07.916
That guy complained about Mani
and got him arrested.

1115
01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:09.416
<i>You just say the word.</i>

1116
01:16:10.041 --> 01:16:12.791
Even we'll file a complaint,
and put him behind bars forever.

1117
01:16:12.875 --> 01:16:15.333
Just let it go. How's dad doing?

1118
01:16:15.416 --> 01:16:17.833
He stole your dad's money.
He betrayed your trust as well.

1119
01:16:17.916 --> 01:16:19.750
<i>And you're asking me to just let it go?</i>

1120
01:16:19.833 --> 01:16:22.208
[sighs] You take care.
I'll call you later.

1121
01:16:25.291 --> 01:16:27.791
[upbeat music playing]

1122
01:16:35.625 --> 01:16:38.083
<i>♪ Let's go where the road takes us ♪</i>

1123
01:16:38.166 --> 01:16:40.708
<i>♪ Travel time to… ♪</i>

1124
01:16:40.791 --> 01:16:43.416
<i>♪ Lost in the city to find ourselves ♪</i>

1125
01:16:43.500 --> 01:16:45.208
<i>♪ Let's go with the flow ♪</i>

1126
01:16:45.291 --> 01:16:48.833
<i>♪ You've got me crazy ♪</i>

1127
01:16:50.958 --> 01:16:56.000
<i>♪ Come, live it up</i>
<i>Let's show the world ♪</i>

1128
01:16:56.083 --> 01:17:01.000
<i>♪ You're on the groove</i>
<i>Show us the moves ♪</i>

1129
01:17:01.083 --> 01:17:03.833
{\an8}<i>♪ We don't know where we're going ♪</i>

1130
01:17:03.916 --> 01:17:06.208
<i>♪ We are on our way ♪</i>

1131
01:17:06.291 --> 01:17:08.166
[singing continues in Tamil]

1132
01:17:40.166 --> 01:17:41.541
[gasps]

1133
01:17:51.000 --> 01:17:52.208
[in Korean] Excuse me!

1134
01:17:52.291 --> 01:17:53.125
Yes.

1135
01:17:54.458 --> 01:17:55.291
This and this.

1136
01:17:55.375 --> 01:17:57.875
-Kimchi fried rice?
-Yes.

1137
01:17:57.958 --> 01:17:59.166
Okay.

1138
01:18:04.041 --> 01:18:05.166
Enjoy your food!

1139
01:18:30.291 --> 01:18:32.375
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

1140
01:18:34.291 --> 01:18:36.791
-May I know who prepared this food?
-It was me.

1141
01:18:36.875 --> 01:18:40.375
-Is there anyone else working for you?
-No, only me.

1142
01:18:46.125 --> 01:18:46.958
It was tasty.

1143
01:18:47.041 --> 01:18:49.208
Thanks.

1144
01:19:31.625 --> 01:19:33.250
[upbeat Tamil folk music playing]

1145
01:19:42.416 --> 01:19:44.916
[imperceptible]

1146
01:20:10.208 --> 01:20:12.333
[in Korean] Guys! Listen to this.

1147
01:20:13.458 --> 01:20:15.833
"Hello! We are the ANI Team at Dream Hive.

1148
01:20:16.625 --> 01:20:19.250
About the short video which you sent us,

1149
01:20:19.333 --> 01:20:22.000
we appreciate your band's teamwork,
music, and talent.

1150
01:20:22.083 --> 01:20:25.208
It grabbed our team's attention.

1151
01:20:25.291 --> 01:20:28.666
We are eager to meet you all soon."

1152
01:20:28.750 --> 01:20:31.916
-[exclaims]
-[all cheering]

1153
01:20:32.000 --> 01:20:32.916
[in English] What?

1154
01:20:34.250 --> 01:20:39.000
Shenba… big music label.

1155
01:20:39.083 --> 01:20:41.458
So many music videos.

1156
01:20:41.541 --> 01:20:42.375
-Meeting, meeting.
-Oh.

1157
01:20:43.041 --> 01:20:47.291
[all cheering]

1158
01:20:48.291 --> 01:20:49.541
Congratulations!

1159
01:20:50.583 --> 01:20:51.583
Congrats!

1160
01:20:51.666 --> 01:20:55.583
[in Korean] Thanks a lot, Shenba.
It's really a miracle.

1161
01:20:55.666 --> 01:20:57.958
So, what should we do now?

1162
01:20:58.041 --> 01:21:01.375
We should start working
to make a music video immediately.

1163
01:21:01.458 --> 01:21:04.875
We need to finetune our music,
visuals, and singing.

1164
01:21:06.041 --> 01:21:08.375
For that, we need a director to help us.

1165
01:21:10.416 --> 01:21:14.375
I know someone.

1166
01:21:15.833 --> 01:21:16.833
Who is that?

1167
01:21:18.666 --> 01:21:19.500
My ex.

1168
01:21:21.916 --> 01:21:24.458
That boy who I slapped?

1169
01:21:26.791 --> 01:21:27.875
Is he a director?

1170
01:21:28.791 --> 01:21:31.541
-Your ex?
-We are done for.

1171
01:21:34.041 --> 01:21:35.166
Jun-Jae.

1172
01:21:38.166 --> 01:21:42.958
Are they okay? They look sad.
Are they okay? Is everything all right?

1173
01:21:43.041 --> 01:21:48.458
[in English] Because we don't have money.
We don't have money to make the video.

1174
01:21:50.208 --> 01:21:53.958
<i>I called up Granny that night.</i>
<i>I wanted to pay my dad back.</i>

1175
01:21:54.041 --> 01:21:57.041
<i>So I'd saved some money</i>
<i>and given it to her for safekeeping.</i>

1176
01:21:57.125 --> 01:21:59.500
<i>I asked her if I could have it back now.</i>

1177
01:21:59.583 --> 01:22:03.083
<i>She laughed and said, "It's your money,</i>
<i>you can do whatever you want."</i>

1178
01:22:03.166 --> 01:22:07.083
<i>Then I told her, "I'm not taking</i>
<i>this money back to give it to my dad.</i>

1179
01:22:07.166 --> 01:22:08.625
<i>I want to give it to the band."</i>

1180
01:22:09.291 --> 01:22:12.750
<i>She said nothing is more important</i>
<i>than my dad and hung up.</i>

1181
01:22:12.833 --> 01:22:17.000
<i>If I were to return the money to my dad,</i>
<i>it would have made me happy.</i>

1182
01:22:17.500 --> 01:22:19.833
<i>But if I were to give the money</i>
<i>to the band,</i>

1183
01:22:19.916 --> 01:22:23.375
<i>it would have helped them</i>
<i>to get to the next stage of their lives.</i>

1184
01:22:23.458 --> 01:22:27.500
<i>But the truth is, I was not demanding</i>
<i>that she give my money back.</i>

1185
01:22:27.583 --> 01:22:30.541
<i>I just wanted her to know that</i>
<i>there is nobody else here</i>

1186
01:22:30.625 --> 01:22:32.041
<i>that I can depend on.</i>

1187
01:22:32.125 --> 01:22:35.625
<i>Besides the money problems, my father</i>
<i>and everything else</i>

1188
01:22:35.708 --> 01:22:37.041
<i>that's happened with me,</i>

1189
01:22:37.125 --> 01:22:39.958
<i>the only thing that mattered</i>
<i>is what she thought of me.</i>

1190
01:22:46.833 --> 01:22:48.666
I'm proud of you.

1191
01:22:58.875 --> 01:23:00.416
[sniffles]

1192
01:23:06.458 --> 01:23:07.625
Why are you crying?

1193
01:23:07.708 --> 01:23:09.041
My dear, don't cry.

1194
01:23:11.541 --> 01:23:12.375
[gasps]

1195
01:23:15.875 --> 01:23:19.083
It's them. Go!

1196
01:23:19.833 --> 01:23:21.625
Money!

1197
01:23:21.708 --> 01:23:23.833
Don't forget the money, it's here!

1198
01:23:23.916 --> 01:23:25.291
Keep it safe!

1199
01:23:27.166 --> 01:23:28.500
[gasps]

1200
01:23:33.916 --> 01:23:34.750
Shenba.

1201
01:23:46.875 --> 01:23:47.958
Sir.

1202
01:23:48.041 --> 01:23:49.250
-Hi, ma'am.
-Shenba.

1203
01:23:49.333 --> 01:23:50.541
Hot water, please.

1204
01:23:50.625 --> 01:23:51.833
Okay.

1205
01:24:11.625 --> 01:24:14.375
-Okay, sir. Okay, ma'am. Bye.
-Shenba.

1206
01:24:15.333 --> 01:24:16.166
Yeah.

1207
01:24:16.875 --> 01:24:18.375
What's in your bag?

1208
01:24:19.833 --> 01:24:21.333
Let me see your bag.

1209
01:24:24.000 --> 01:24:25.208
Let me see your bag.

1210
01:24:25.833 --> 01:24:27.000
Ma'am! Ma'am!

1211
01:24:31.958 --> 01:24:33.708
-Ma'am.
-Whose money?

1212
01:24:33.791 --> 01:24:35.958
Whose money? [in Korean] Honey.

1213
01:24:36.041 --> 01:24:38.791
I knew it. I told you something felt off.

1214
01:24:38.875 --> 01:24:42.583
[in English] Ma'am, this is mine.
This is mine, ma'am.

1215
01:24:42.666 --> 01:24:44.916
-You steal this from my house?
-No, sir.

1216
01:24:45.000 --> 01:24:47.375
[in Korean] She's such a thief.
A complete thief…

1217
01:24:47.458 --> 01:24:50.541
-Sir, is this my money.
-Whose money is this? Whose money?

1218
01:24:50.625 --> 01:24:52.041
-Sir, sir, it's my money.
-Thief.

1219
01:24:52.583 --> 01:24:54.291
[in English] What's this?

1220
01:24:54.375 --> 01:24:56.250
-Ma'am.
-[yells] What's going on?

1221
01:24:56.333 --> 01:24:57.708
[in Korean] Shut up!

1222
01:25:10.416 --> 01:25:13.208
This is Shenba's money.
Give it back right now.

1223
01:25:16.541 --> 01:25:17.458
What the heck?

1224
01:25:18.583 --> 01:25:20.125
What do you think you're doing?

1225
01:25:20.666 --> 01:25:21.500
Eh?

1226
01:25:22.625 --> 01:25:25.458
Mom, have you been deceiving us
this whole time?

1227
01:25:26.583 --> 01:25:31.458
You've acted like you couldn't move
while planning this behind our back?

1228
01:25:32.125 --> 01:25:34.583
Who gave you the right
to talk to me like that?

1229
01:25:34.666 --> 01:25:36.875
Have you ever treated me like your mom?

1230
01:25:37.916 --> 01:25:40.666
What do you mean,
I didn't treat you like my mom?

1231
01:25:41.833 --> 01:25:42.958
Think carefully.

1232
01:25:43.041 --> 01:25:45.541
-Think carefully.
-Whatever.

1233
01:25:46.416 --> 01:25:47.791
Pack your things now.

1234
01:25:47.875 --> 01:25:50.125
Get out of my house.
You're going to Busan.

1235
01:25:50.208 --> 01:25:53.000
Shenba! [in English] Get out, now!

1236
01:25:54.125 --> 01:25:55.333
Get out now!

1237
01:26:00.541 --> 01:26:01.375
Shenba.

1238
01:26:03.500 --> 01:26:04.875
Take your money.

1239
01:26:09.625 --> 01:26:11.375
It's your money. Go.

1240
01:26:13.000 --> 01:26:13.875
Go!

1241
01:26:24.208 --> 01:26:27.375
[in Korean] What are you doing?
Why would you give that money to her?

1242
01:26:27.458 --> 01:26:30.375
That's Shenba's money. She earned it!

1243
01:26:30.458 --> 01:26:31.291
Ah.

1244
01:26:35.791 --> 01:26:36.791
So that's why

1245
01:26:38.166 --> 01:26:41.041
you lied to us
while running this restaurant.

1246
01:26:41.125 --> 01:26:44.083
You became a kitchen worker again
and wore this around?

1247
01:26:44.791 --> 01:26:46.750
I raised you by working in the kitchen.

1248
01:26:46.833 --> 01:26:49.375
That "kitchen worker"
gave you an education!

1249
01:26:49.458 --> 01:26:52.500
That's why you should rest!

1250
01:26:52.583 --> 01:26:54.958
Just take care of the kids and rest!

1251
01:26:55.041 --> 01:26:56.958
I don't want to!

1252
01:26:57.041 --> 01:26:59.083
I have my own things I want to do!

1253
01:27:00.041 --> 01:27:01.916
[breathing heavily]

1254
01:27:03.958 --> 01:27:05.875
[sniffles, sobs]

1255
01:27:07.583 --> 01:27:09.041
We also…

1256
01:27:10.166 --> 01:27:11.916
have things we want to do.

1257
01:27:21.166 --> 01:27:24.333
We have to work too, you know.

1258
01:27:28.083 --> 01:27:30.208
Why do you keep working…

1259
01:27:31.041 --> 01:27:32.541
[exclaims] Mom!

1260
01:27:35.125 --> 01:27:36.833
[siren wailing]

1261
01:27:37.583 --> 01:27:39.083
[somber music playing]

1262
01:28:11.083 --> 01:28:12.333
Yeon-Ok…

1263
01:28:13.000 --> 01:28:14.791
Can you please help?
I need to see Yeon-Ok.

1264
01:28:14.875 --> 01:28:16.541
-Yeon-Ok? Okay, wait.
-Yeah, Yeon-Ok, yeah.

1265
01:28:17.041 --> 01:28:18.083
Please.

1266
01:28:20.708 --> 01:28:22.625
-Just there.
-Thank you.

1267
01:28:27.375 --> 01:28:29.958
-Sir, please.
-Why you come to here?

1268
01:28:30.041 --> 01:28:33.916
-Sir, please, sir, one minute.
-Go! No, no!

1269
01:28:34.000 --> 01:28:36.083
-Can I just see her once, please, sir.
-Get out, now!

1270
01:28:36.833 --> 01:28:37.958
-Get out!
-Sir, please.

1271
01:28:38.041 --> 01:28:41.666
-Ma'am, one minute, ma'am. Please.
-Shenba. Get out!

1272
01:28:42.291 --> 01:28:43.875
-Sir, don't do this, please.
-Get out now.

1273
01:28:43.958 --> 01:28:46.791
If I see you here again,
I will call the police.

1274
01:28:46.875 --> 01:28:48.208
Sir!

1275
01:28:48.291 --> 01:28:49.500
[sobs]

1276
01:28:50.750 --> 01:28:52.000
Shenba.

1277
01:28:55.625 --> 01:28:56.458
[sighs]

1278
01:29:13.625 --> 01:29:15.958
This is how I saw you for the first time.

1279
01:29:17.500 --> 01:29:19.541
But I didn't feel like crying then.

1280
01:29:22.583 --> 01:29:24.333
I can't see you like this.

1281
01:29:26.000 --> 01:29:27.583
I'm very scared.

1282
01:29:30.666 --> 01:29:32.833
I don't want anything to happen to you.

1283
01:29:34.375 --> 01:29:35.625
Nothing.

1284
01:29:38.583 --> 01:29:40.750
Please forgive me
if I've ever wronged you.

1285
01:29:47.333 --> 01:29:49.541
[soaring Tamil music playing]

1286
01:30:28.125 --> 01:30:31.583
<i>Without knowing if I'd ever be able</i>
<i>to see her again,</i>

1287
01:30:31.666 --> 01:30:33.458
<i>I left the hospital.</i>

1288
01:30:41.291 --> 01:30:46.208
<i>Sometimes, you just can't express</i>
<i>the pain that's inside you to anyone.</i>

1289
01:30:46.291 --> 01:30:48.541
<i>And that's the greatest pain.</i>

1290
01:30:59.666 --> 01:31:01.875
[bell rings]

1291
01:31:17.708 --> 01:31:18.875
Shenba…

1292
01:31:19.750 --> 01:31:21.375
are you okay?

1293
01:31:28.833 --> 01:31:30.625
Here's the money for your music video.

1294
01:31:35.375 --> 01:31:37.000
[both cheering]

1295
01:31:37.083 --> 01:31:39.333
[in Korean] I think we can film it now.

1296
01:31:41.333 --> 01:31:43.208
[in English] Thank you so much, Shenba!

1297
01:31:44.541 --> 01:31:48.916
I know this money is
very important for you.

1298
01:31:49.000 --> 01:31:51.041
But you helped us, thank you.

1299
01:31:57.583 --> 01:31:58.833
[upbeat K-pop music playing]

1300
01:32:22.708 --> 01:32:23.916
Quick make-up touch up.

1301
01:32:43.833 --> 01:32:45.333
Ji-min!

1302
01:32:59.375 --> 01:33:00.833
Okay!

1303
01:34:25.583 --> 01:34:26.625
[cell phone chimes]

1304
01:34:45.291 --> 01:34:46.583
[intense music playing]

1305
01:35:08.208 --> 01:35:11.875
{\an8}[female news announcer] <i>Massive landslide</i>
<i>strikes Kolappalur after heavy rains.</i>

1306
01:35:11.958 --> 01:35:15.083
{\an8}<i>Several homes destroyed.</i>
<i>Rescue operations intensified.</i>

1307
01:35:15.166 --> 01:35:18.333
{\an8}<i>Kolappalur was severely affected</i>
<i>by a massive landslide</i>

1308
01:35:18.416 --> 01:35:20.291
{\an8}<i>triggered by continuous heavy rainfall,</i>

1309
01:35:20.375 --> 01:35:24.500
{\an8}causing widespread destruction to homes,
roads and agricultural land.

1310
01:35:24.583 --> 01:35:28.666
<i>The landslide occurred in the early hours,</i>
<i>catching many residents off-guard</i>

1311
01:35:28.750 --> 01:35:31.458
<i>and forcing families</i>
<i>to flee their homes in fear.</i>

1312
01:35:31.541 --> 01:35:35.791
<i>Local authorities reported that several</i>
<i>homes were either completely destroyed</i>

1313
01:35:35.875 --> 01:35:39.000
<i>or partially damaged,</i>
<i>leaving many families homeless.</i>

1314
01:35:39.083 --> 01:35:41.708
<i>Roads connecting interior villages</i>
<i>were blocked</i>

1315
01:35:41.791 --> 01:35:44.583
<i>due to fallen debris,</i>
<i>mud and uprooted trees,</i>

1316
01:35:44.666 --> 01:35:47.833
<i>disrupting transportation</i>
<i>and emergency access.</i>

1317
01:37:10.041 --> 01:37:13.208
What's going on? Stop faffing around.
Come on, hurry up.

1318
01:37:24.500 --> 01:37:26.750
I've been noticing something
since you're back.

1319
01:37:26.833 --> 01:37:29.250
You look quite unhappy. What's wrong?

1320
01:37:30.250 --> 01:37:31.416
Mmm.

1321
01:37:32.291 --> 01:37:33.416
[sighs]

1322
01:37:34.291 --> 01:37:37.208
I've been wanting to tell you something
for a very long time.

1323
01:37:38.125 --> 01:37:40.208
You don't file a police complaint
against Mani.

1324
01:37:40.291 --> 01:37:43.375
He's not been the same since.
He's a changed man now.

1325
01:37:45.208 --> 01:37:48.458
He was begging me to give him
your phone number, so I…

1326
01:37:48.541 --> 01:37:51.333
I thought you would give him
a piece of your mind, so I gave him.

1327
01:37:53.541 --> 01:37:54.500
[clicks tongue]

1328
01:37:54.583 --> 01:37:57.250
And not just that,
when the landslide happened,

1329
01:37:57.333 --> 01:37:59.208
I wasn't there to help your parents.

1330
01:37:59.291 --> 01:38:02.958
He was the one who made sure
that they get to the relief camp safely.

1331
01:38:17.000 --> 01:38:20.166
<i>I mean, I'm not saying</i>
<i>that you forgive him.</i>

1332
01:38:20.250 --> 01:38:22.000
Just talk to him once.

1333
01:38:22.708 --> 01:38:24.833
{\an8}[cell phone ringing]

1334
01:38:27.791 --> 01:38:29.666
{\an8}Who is it? Is it that jerk?

1335
01:38:30.916 --> 01:38:32.000
Who else?

1336
01:38:33.041 --> 01:38:34.541
It's from Korea.

1337
01:38:34.625 --> 01:38:36.458
Then why didn't you just answer the phone?

1338
01:38:38.166 --> 01:38:39.958
-I didn't want to answer.
-Why?

1339
01:38:40.041 --> 01:38:42.375
If I speak to them,
I'll feel like going back.

1340
01:38:42.958 --> 01:38:46.208
With what's happened here,
[clicks tongue] I can't.

1341
01:39:00.541 --> 01:39:03.416
[automated voice]
<i>The number you are trying to call is busy.</i>

1342
01:39:07.041 --> 01:39:08.125
Shenba.

1343
01:39:14.166 --> 01:39:15.875
Can I talk to you for a minute?

1344
01:39:19.416 --> 01:39:20.666
Shenba…

1345
01:39:34.375 --> 01:39:36.625
I tried to get in touch
with you many times.

1346
01:39:37.583 --> 01:39:41.458
And I just wanted to say that I'll return
your dad's money somehow.

1347
01:39:41.541 --> 01:39:43.083
But you didn't talk to me.

1348
01:39:44.791 --> 01:39:49.833
I was not calling you for your forgiveness
or for you to take me back,

1349
01:39:50.750 --> 01:39:52.333
even if you forgive me.

1350
01:39:53.541 --> 01:39:55.333
I'll never forgive myself.

1351
01:39:57.958 --> 01:39:59.208
I wanted to…

1352
01:40:00.833 --> 01:40:02.750
meet you and apologize.

1353
01:40:07.958 --> 01:40:09.125
Sorry.

1354
01:40:09.208 --> 01:40:10.500
[soaring music playing]

1355
01:40:17.166 --> 01:40:21.166
Say whatever you want to,
but I have just one thing to say.

1356
01:40:22.833 --> 01:40:23.708
Thanks.

1357
01:40:26.583 --> 01:40:27.916
It's all because of you.

1358
01:40:29.958 --> 01:40:30.916
Thanks.

1359
01:41:00.958 --> 01:41:02.125
<i>Hi, Shenba.</i>

1360
01:41:03.083 --> 01:41:06.291
<i>Without saying anything,</i>
<i>you went to your hometown.</i>

1361
01:41:23.208 --> 01:41:25.916
<i>The first time I saw you at the airport,</i>

1362
01:41:26.000 --> 01:41:28.250
<i>you were standing there</i>
<i>with tears in your eyes.</i>

1363
01:41:28.333 --> 01:41:31.375
<i>I don't know why, but something</i>
<i>made me want to reach out,</i>

1364
01:41:31.458 --> 01:41:32.416
<i>to talk to you,</i>

1365
01:41:33.375 --> 01:41:34.625
<i>to help you.</i>

1366
01:41:34.708 --> 01:41:37.083
<i>Now I find myself missing you deeply.</i>

1367
01:41:38.291 --> 01:41:39.666
<i>See you soon.</i>

1368
01:41:40.375 --> 01:41:41.208
<i>Bye.</i>

1369
01:41:43.250 --> 01:41:45.375
[violin playing]

1370
01:42:33.166 --> 01:42:35.500
[upbeat music playing]

1371
01:43:19.625 --> 01:43:21.083
What's on your mind?

1372
01:43:21.166 --> 01:43:22.666
Don't over think.

1373
01:43:22.750 --> 01:43:25.041
Whatever your heart says, just do it.

1374
01:43:25.583 --> 01:43:30.000
Your Korean friends keep asking me,
"Sir, can you send Shenba back with us?"

1375
01:43:30.083 --> 01:43:31.541
I told them to talk to you.

1376
01:43:31.625 --> 01:43:33.875
And yeah, what did you say to your mother?

1377
01:43:33.958 --> 01:43:36.625
"The money I took from Dad,
I'll pay him back one day."

1378
01:43:36.708 --> 01:43:38.541
You said you don't have it right now?

1379
01:43:39.500 --> 01:43:42.416
Even if you managed
to pay me back the money somehow,

1380
01:43:42.500 --> 01:43:44.750
it wouldn't make me so happy.

1381
01:43:44.833 --> 01:43:47.291
I'm very happy today, you know why?

1382
01:43:47.875 --> 01:43:52.250
Four people just came to see you,
that too from across the world.

1383
01:43:52.333 --> 01:43:54.041
This makes me really happy.

1384
01:43:54.125 --> 01:43:56.833
Why don't you do one thing?
Go back to Korea.

1385
01:43:56.916 --> 01:44:00.083
Call me and then I'll come
with your mother.

1386
01:44:00.166 --> 01:44:01.750
You don't mind that, do you?

1387
01:44:03.708 --> 01:44:06.125
Go ahead and live your dream life.

1388
01:44:30.791 --> 01:44:32.833
[plane engine whirring]

1389
01:44:39.166 --> 01:44:41.250
[soaring music playing]

1390
01:44:44.833 --> 01:44:45.666
HOUSE FOR RENT
230 MILLION WON

1391
01:45:32.708 --> 01:45:34.125
[bell tinkling]

1392
01:46:11.291 --> 01:46:12.416
How is she?

1393
01:46:12.500 --> 01:46:13.333
Um…

1394
01:46:14.666 --> 01:46:17.333
She want to… you hear this.

1395
01:46:20.625 --> 01:46:22.750
[automated voice]
<i>Hi, Shenba, how are you doing?</i>

1396
01:46:22.833 --> 01:46:25.583
<i>I wanted to talk to you</i>
<i>and share my feelings with you.</i>

1397
01:46:25.666 --> 01:46:28.000
<i>The time I spent with you was beautiful,</i>

1398
01:46:28.083 --> 01:46:31.250
{\an8}<i>I laughed a lot</i>
<i>and I could be myself with you.</i>

1399
01:46:31.333 --> 01:46:33.916
{\an8}<i>The best thing</i>
<i>was that my dream came true,</i>

1400
01:46:34.000 --> 01:46:38.666
<i>my dream of opening a restaurant</i>
<i>which became possible only because of you.</i>

1401
01:46:38.750 --> 01:46:42.166
<i>After a long time,</i>
<i>I felt a connection with someone.</i>

1402
01:46:42.250 --> 01:46:44.333
<i>And that was with you, Shenba.</i>

1403
01:46:45.541 --> 01:46:49.125
<i>You are like my own daughter.</i>
<i>I'll always be there for you.</i>

1404
01:46:50.666 --> 01:46:53.875
[continues speaking in Korean]

1405
01:46:59.958 --> 01:47:02.166
<i>I hope we meet again soon.</i>

1406
01:47:16.333 --> 01:47:17.875
I want to talk to her.

1407
01:47:21.333 --> 01:47:23.791
[ekg beeping]

1408
01:47:24.708 --> 01:47:26.500
[rapidly beeping]

1409
01:47:28.541 --> 01:47:29.750
She is no more.

1410
01:48:08.291 --> 01:48:10.041
[bell tinkling]

1411
01:48:12.250 --> 01:48:15.333
<i>I've always dreamed of visiting Korea,</i>

1412
01:48:15.416 --> 01:48:19.041
<i>and that dream was the only connection</i>
<i>I had with this country.</i>

1413
01:48:20.375 --> 01:48:23.416
<i>A few days ago,</i>
<i>if anyone asked me who I was,</i>

1414
01:48:23.500 --> 01:48:24.875
<i>I wouldn't know what to say.</i>

1415
01:48:24.958 --> 01:48:28.500
<i>But today, I'd say I'm from Shenba</i>
<i>from Granny's Kitchen,</i>

1416
01:48:28.583 --> 01:48:30.000
<i>this is my identity.</i>

1417
01:48:30.083 --> 01:48:32.583
{\an8}<i>They say where you think it ends,</i>
<i>it begins.</i>

1418
01:48:32.666 --> 01:48:36.208
{\an8}<i>Just like that, when I thought</i>
<i>everything was over for me here,</i>

1419
01:48:36.291 --> 01:48:38.666
{\an8}<i>everything was actually just beginning.</i>

1420
01:48:39.875 --> 01:48:41.708
[soaring music playing]

1421
01:49:11.541 --> 01:49:13.166
[K-pop music playing]
